    ],
    "title": "## 1. System Paradigm & Repository Layout",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5P0004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5P0004",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA5P0005"
    ],
    "title": "### Architectural Paradigm",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5P0005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5P0005",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA5P0006",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA5P8000"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C64YWET0005",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5P0006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5P0006",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA5P0007"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWET0006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5P0007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5P0007",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Apeiron (Fluid Core Substrate)**: Schema-free semantic continuum — Markdown content as an unbounded fractal tree, not a fixed document/block hierarchy.",
    "title": "00C64YWET0007",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5P8000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5P8000",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA5P8001"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWET0008",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5P8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5P8001",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Peras (Crystallized Interfaces)**: Typed boundary structures. As of the fractal-ontology redesign, the whole `BlockNode` tree is eagerly parsed and committed on ingest, each block assigned a Snowflake-generated identity independent of its content or offsets, rather than reified lazily on-demand — the on-demand-reification mechanism (`SpanNode`, character-offset spans) described in earlier revisions of this doc was eliminated, not merely deferred.",
    "title": "00C64YWET0009",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5P8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5P8002",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET000B"
    ],
    "title": "### Directory Structure: Core vs Community Boundaries",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5P8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5P8003",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```\nAperas/                               # Core Engine (Maintained by Core Dev Team)\n├── scripts/                          # Universal infrastructure & DB operational tooling\n│   ├── restore.sh                    # Backup, restore & verification suite\n│   ├── tdb-log.sh                    # Local-time commit log helper (default count: 20)\n│   └── tdb-doc.sh                    # Local-time document inspection helper\n├── skills/                           # Core agent skill definitions\n│   └── terminusdb/                   # TerminusDB operational reference skill\n├── web/                              # TypeScript project for substrate transducers & UI\n│   └── src/lib/                      # Core data access, AST transducer & schema modules\n│\n└── AperasKG/                         # Domain KG (Maintained by Community)\n    ├── artifacts/                    # Plain-text Markdown domain projections & documentation\n    ├── schema/                       # Domain-specific JSON-LD schemas extending core\n    ├── ontology/                     # Domain-specific predicate taxonomy / vocabularies\n    └── transducers/                  # Domain-specific ingestion/parsing scripts\n```",
    "title": "00C5FPA5P8003",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG000",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG001",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG002",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG003",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG006"
    ],
    "title": "## 2. Canonical Data Substrate & Schema",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG001",
    "children": [],
    "text": "The canonical schema is implemented in `web/src/lib/schema.json` (pure JSON-LD, no longer duplicated as TypeScript interfaces) using a fractal, content-addressed class lineage — see `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` for the full rationale:",
    "title": "00C64YWET000D",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG002",
    "children": [],
    "text": "| JSON-LD Class | Key Strategy | Core Fields | Purpose |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `BaseNode` | — (abstract) | `links: Set<BaseLink>` | Root of all addressable content; owns intrinsic links. |\n| `BaseLink` | — (abstract) | `target: BaseNode`, `predicate` | Intrinsic connection authored inside a node. |\n| `BaseEdge` | — (abstract) | `source: BaseNode` (+ `BaseLink` fields) | Extrinsic assertion, independently authored/floating. |\n| `Assertion` | — (concrete, no own fields) | inherits `BaseEdge` | The one concrete extrinsic-edge leaf type — `BaseEdge` is abstract, so something instantiable is needed to actually write edges like `impacts`/`verifies`/`affects`. See `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §2.C. |\n| `BlockNode` | Lexical (`blockId`, Snowflake-generated) | `blockId`, `title`, `text`, `children: List<BlockNode>`, `unfolded` | Fractal content atom — a document is just the root `BlockNode` of its `ArtifactNode`; no separate `DocumentNode`. |\n| `ArtifactNode` | Lexical (`path`) | `path`, `fileHash`, `lastTrackedAt`, `ingestedHash`, `lastIngestedAt`, `root: BlockNode` | Metadata index for tracking repository files and hash deltas; anchors the fractal tree. `fileHash`/`ingestedHash` are flat file-content hashes, not structural — see `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §1.B. |\n| `FolderNode` | Lexical (`path`) | `title`, `path`, `text`, `children: List<BaseNode>` | Structural container mirroring a directory under `AperasKG/artifacts/`; absorbs its own `README.md` (never exposed as a separate `ArtifactNode`) and references nested `FolderNode`s/`ArtifactNode`s by id. See `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §4.A. |",
    "title": "00C64YWET000E",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG003",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG004",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG005"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWET8000",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG004",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Design note**: `BlockNode` identity is a Snowflake-style generated id (see `web/src/lib/snowflake.ts`), not a content hash — decoupling node identity from content fingerprinting was the resolution to the identity/dedup conflation documented in `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` Appendix F.",
    "title": "00C64YWET8001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG005",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Superseded**: `DocumentNode`, `SpanNode`, and `TripleAssertion` (Lexical/Random-keyed, positional `blockId`s) were the Phase 0 schema before this redesign — eliminated entirely, not merely renamed.",
    "title": "00C64YWET8002",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG006",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG007"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWET8003",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG007",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Schema Protocol Requirement**: Schema initialization uses `full_replace` for idempotent updates. The submitted schema array **must include an explicit `@context` document** (`@base: \"terminusdb:///data/\"`, `@schema: \"terminusdb:///schema#\"`), or the server will reject the replacement.",
    "title": "00C64YWET8004",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG008",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET8006",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG00A"
    ],
    "title": "## 3. Data Access & Transduction Modules",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG009",
    "children": [],
    "text": "| Module | Location | Responsibilities & Protocol Constraints |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Client Manager** | `web/src/lib/client.ts` | Configures `TerminusDB.WOQLClient`, creates `aperas_apeiron` database, applies idempotent schema initialization via `full_replace` from `schema.json`. |\n| **Node Identity** | `web/src/lib/snowflake.ts` | Generates the 64-bit Snowflake-style `blockId` (timestamp + machine identity + sequence, 13-char Crockford Base32) — see `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §1.A. |\n| **AST Transducer** | `web/src/lib/astParser.ts` | Uses `unified.js` (`remark-parse`) to recursively convert Markdown into a nested `BlockNode` tree, assigning each block a fresh Snowflake id via `snowflake.ts` (identity is never derived from content or position). |\n| **Artifact Tracking & Ingestion** | `web/src/lib/artifacts.ts` | Computes `fileHash`, tracks/upserts lightweight `ArtifactNode`s, and ingests the full `BlockNode` tree on change — see §4 below. |\n| **Folder Ingestion** | `web/src/lib/folders.ts` | Walks `AperasKG/artifacts/` and commits the `FolderNode` structural tree — see §4 below. |\n| **Extrinsic Assertion CRUD** | `web/src/lib/crud.ts` | `insertAssertion`/`deleteAssertionsInvolvingNode` for the concrete `Assertion` type (source/predicate/target, node-typed per §3 of the design doc's rejection of the `xsd:string` anti-pattern), plus generic best-effort document delete helpers. |\n| **WOQL Engine** | `web/src/lib/woql.ts` | Builds and executes WOQL queries over `Assertion` — `queryNodeAssertions` (both directions) and `traceImpactPropagation` (one-hop sweep along a predicate like `impacts`). |\n| **GraphQL Client** | `web/src/lib/graphql.ts` | `getArtifactTreeViaGraphQL` fetches an `ArtifactNode` and its full nested `BlockNode` tree (bounded depth) via the auto-generated GraphQL endpoint — see the note below on why this is the *only* full-tree read path. |\n| **Version Control** | `web/src/lib/versionControl.ts` | Manages branches, temporal commit histories, version diffing, merge applications (`apply`), and state resets. Class-agnostic — unaffected by the schema redesign. |",
    "title": "00C5FPA5PG009",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG00A",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG00B"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWET8007",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG00B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG00B",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Read-path note**: `client.getDocument()` on an `ArtifactNode` returns `root` as a bare reference id string, not the nested tree, and likewise for `BlockNode.children`. This is *not* because `@subdocument` is required for unfolding (a natural-sounding but wrong assumption we initially made) — it's simply that `BlockNode` isn't schema-annotated as unfoldable. TerminusDB has two independent schema-level annotations that control this: property-level `\"@unfold\": true` and class-level `\"@unfoldable\": []`. We benchmarked marking `BlockNode` class-level `@unfoldable` (which does work, including through the recursive `List<BlockNode>` children) against the real 149-block `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` tree, and it was ~3.5x slower than `getArtifactTreeViaGraphQL`'s GraphQL query (~48ms vs ~13.5ms steady-state) — so we kept GraphQL as the tree-read path rather than adopting it. Separately, we found that the *property-level* `\"@unfold\": true` variant silently does nothing on `List`-typed fields specifically (works on `Set`/`Optional`/`Cardinality`) — an upstream bug, filed as [terminusdb/terminusdb#2512](https://github.com/terminusdb/terminusdb/issues/2512), traced to `List`'s internal RDF-linked-list (`Cons`/`rdf:first`/`rdf:rest`) representation not being reachable from the property-level unfold check. That bug doesn't affect our decision (we'd have used class-level `@unfoldable`, which is unaffected), but is a useful data point that this part of TerminusDB is new and still maturing.",
    "title": "00C64YWET8008",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG00C",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG00D",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG00E"
    ],
    "title": "## 4. Artifact Tracking & Ingestion Pipeline",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG00D",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Managed via `web/src/lib/artifacts.ts` and CLI entrypoint `web/src/lib/kgCli.ts`:",
    "title": "00C64YWET800A",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG00E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG00E",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG00F",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG00H"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C64YWET800B",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG00F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG00F",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG00G"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWET800C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG00G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG00G",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Lightweight Registration (`npm run kg:track`)**:\n  Computes content hashes for files under `AperasKG/artifacts/` and upserts lightweight `ArtifactNode` records — a no-op skip (no KG write at all) when the hash is unchanged, so unscoped sweeps (e.g. the `post-index-change` hook) stay cheap.",
    "title": "00C64YWET800D",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG00H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG00H",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG00J"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWET800E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG00J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG00J",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Incremental Ingestion (`npm run kg:ingest`)**:\n  Compares current file content hash (`fileHash`) against stored `ingestedHash`. If changed, parses Markdown into a nested `BlockNode` tree (fresh Snowflake ids throughout) and commits it via a single `ArtifactNode.root` update — TerminusDB recursively ingests the whole tree in one operation. Re-ingesting an already-ingested artifact currently orphans its entire previous tree rather than reusing unchanged blocks' ids — acceptable for now since ingestion targets uningested artifacts; cross-ingestion identity matching is unimplemented (see `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` Appendix F).\n  Also rebuilds the `FolderNode` structural tree (`web/src/lib/folders.ts`) in the same run: one `FolderNode` per directory under `AperasKG/artifacts/`, each absorbing its own `README.md` (parsed blocks become the folder's own children; the file itself is never exposed as a separate `ArtifactNode`) and referencing nested `FolderNode`s/`ArtifactNode`s by id. The whole folder tree is committed as a single nested write from the artifacts root each run — cheap, since it's directory-count-sized, not content-sized.",
    "title": "00C64YWET800F",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG00K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG00K",
    "children": [],
    "title": "## 5. Backup, Disaster Recovery & Synchronization Strategy",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG00M",
