    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG00Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG00Y",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FPA5PG00Y",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG00Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG00Z",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Mechanism**: Wraps TerminusDB `bundle` / `unbundle` CLI commands. `backup` self-verifies by unbundling into a temporary verification database.",
    "title": "00C5FPA5PG00Z",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG010",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FPA5PG010",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG011",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG011",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Scope**: **Same-instance snapshot & local rollback only**. CLI `.bundle` exports suffer from cross-store layer reference incompatibility (issue #2509) and cannot be transferred across independent TerminusDB server instances.",
    "title": "00C5FPA5PG011",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG012",
    "children": [],
    "title": "## 6. SSH-Tunneled Remotes",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG013",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG013",
    "children": [],
    "text": "TerminusDB remotes communicate over HTTP REST endpoints. Cross-machine communication between separate hosts utilizes SSH local port forwarding:",
    "title": "00C5FPA5PG013",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG014",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG014",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FPA5PG014",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG015",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG015",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FPA5PG015",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG016",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG016",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Transport Rationale**: Native remote commands (`push`/`pull`/`fetch`/`clone`) speak HTTP(S) only. TerminusDB itself listens on `0.0.0.0:6363` inside the container (confirmed via `/proc/net/tcp`) — the loopback-only restriction (`127.0.0.1:6363`) is this project's own `docker run -p 127.0.0.1:6363:6363` deployment choice, not a TerminusDB default. Either way, this project's containers are loopback-only, so cross-machine transport requires an SSH tunnel.",
    "title": "00C5FPA5PG016",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG017",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG017",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FPA5PG017",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG018",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG018",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Tunnel Endpoint**: `ssh -N -f -L 0.0.0.0:6364:localhost:6363 <user>@<remote-host>`",
    "title": "00C5FPA5PG018",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG019",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG019",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FPA5PG019",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG01A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG01A",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Firewall Access**: `sudo ufw allow from 172.17.0.0/16 to any port 6364 proto tcp`",
    "title": "00C5FPA5PG01A",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG01B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG01B",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FPA5PG01B",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG01C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG01C",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Bridge Addressing**: Remote URLs target the host's Docker bridge gateway (`http://172.17.0.1:6364/admin/aperas_apeiron`).",
    "title": "00C5FPA5PG01C",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG01D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG01D",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FPA5PG01D",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG01E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG01E",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Remote Tracking**: `fetch` updates local remote-tracking descriptors (`<org>/<db>/<remote>/branch/<branch>`). `fetch` must be executed before `push` or `pull` can resolve remote heads.",
    "title": "00C5FPA5PG01E",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG01F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG01F",
    "children": [],
    "title": "## 7. Verification & Operational Utilities",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG01G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG01G",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FPA5PG01G",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG01H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG01H",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FPA5PG01H",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG01J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG01J",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Verification Test Harness**: `npm run verify:phase0 -- --db` (`web/src/lib/verifyPhase0.ts`) — end-to-end, idempotent, self-cleaning live test: AST parsing, schema init, artifact track/ingest, GraphQL tree read, `FolderNode` ingestion, `Assertion` CRUD + WOQL impact propagation, and temporal commit management (branch + commit log). Demo-state cleanup has to happen in reference-reversed order — `FolderNode` before `ArtifactNode` before its `BlockNode`s — since TerminusDB enforces referential integrity and rejects deleting a still-referenced document.",
    "title": "00C5FPA5PG01J",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG01K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG01K",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FPA5PG01K",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG01M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG01M",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**`Aperas/scripts/tdb-log.sh`**: Provides compact, local-time commit history (`--count 20` by default) with fast client-side message filtering (`--filter`). Avoids sluggish `tdb history` diffs.",
    "title": "00C5FPA5PG01M",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG01N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG01N",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FPA5PG01N",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA5PG01P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA5PG01P",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**`Aperas/scripts/tdb-doc.sh`**: Wraps `tdb doc get` to convert ISO UTC timestamps to local time and unescape literal newlines (`\\n`) into readable multi-line prose.",
    "title": "00C5FPA5PG01P",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:19.881Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R000",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R001"
    ],
    "title": "Document Root",
    "type": "root",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R001",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R002",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R003",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00X",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01N",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R025",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03A",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R047"
    ],
    "title": "# Aperas Core Ontology Design",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R002",
    "children": [],
    "text": "This document defines the core semantic graph ontology for Aperas. It establishes mathematically rigorous identity, strong polymorphic typing, and universal addressability for all graph components.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R002",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R003",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R004",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R005",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00K"
    ],
    "title": "## 1. Node Identity vs. Content Fingerprint",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R004",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Addressable components (e.g., `BlockNode`) require stable identities that survive re-ingestion. Because identity must remain constant across edits while content-change detection must reflect every edit, these concerns are handled by two separate fields (see Appendix F for why a single-hash design failed).",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R004",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R005",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R006",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R007",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R008",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R009",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00A",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00B",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00J"
    ],
    "title": "### A. Node Identity (Stable, Content-Independent)",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R006",
    "children": [],
    "text": "A `BlockNode`'s `@id` is a **Snowflake-style generated identifier**. It is assigned once at creation and is fully decoupled from the node's content and position, ensuring that `BaseLink` and `BaseEdge` assertions survive edits to their referenced nodes.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R006",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R007",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**64-bit Layout**: Encoded as a 13-character Crockford Base32 string. It is compact and lexicographically sortable by creation time.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R007",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R008",
    "children": [],
    "text": "| Field | Bits | Purpose |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Sign** | 1 | Unused. Keeps value a positive signed int64 for cross-language compatibility. |\n| **Timestamp** | 45 | Milliseconds since custom epoch (e.g., 2025-01-01) — provides ~1,115 years of range. |\n| **Machine ID** | 10 | 1 anomaly-flag bit + 9 machine-number bits — supports 512 machines with personal failover identities. |\n| **Sequence** | 8 | Per-machine-identity counter, reset each millisecond — allows 256 ids/ms/machine. |",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R008",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R009",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Deterministic Collision Avoidance**: \nCollisions are prevented by construction rather than probability. Timestamps separate different times, the sequence counter disambiguates same-millisecond generation on one machine, and the machine ID separates different machines.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R009",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R00A",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Handling Local Clock Anomalies (NTP corrections)**:",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R00A",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R00B",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00C",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00E",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00G"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R00B",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R00C",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00D"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R00D",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Prevention**: NTP uses gradual \"slew\" adjustments instead of \"step\" (instant jumps).",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R00D",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R00E",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00F"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R00E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R00F",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Absorption**: The generator uses a high-water-mark (`max(now, last_emitted)`). Small backward jumps are absorbed by the sequence counter.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R00F",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R00G",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00H"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R00G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R00H",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Failover**: If a backward jump is too large (risking counter overflow), the generator flips its anomaly bit to use a distinct failover machine ID, preventing collisions with its normal output.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R00H",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R00J",
    "children": [],
    "text": "*(Note: While extreme, unbounded backward jumps under sustained load remain theoretically possible, they require deliberate clock tampering.)*",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R00J",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R00K",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00M",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00N",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00P",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00V",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00W"
    ],
    "title": "### B. Content Fingerprint & Reconciliation",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R00M",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Once a `BlockNode` tree is ingested into the database, **the DB becomes the source of truth**. Edits are made directly in the DB, and artifact files are regenerated (projected) from it. Re-ingestion is a **fallback reconciliation path**, triggered only when an external hand-edit causes the file to drift from its projected state.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R00M",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R00N",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Minimal Fingerprinting on `ArtifactNode`**:\nOnly two flat, file-level hashes are maintained (no structural hashes):",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R00N",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R00P",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00Q",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00S"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R00P",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R00Q",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00R"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R00Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R00R",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**`fileHash`**: Hash of the raw file's current content, recomputed on every `track` event.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R00R",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R00S",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00T"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R00S",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R00T",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**`ingestedHash`**: Hash of the raw file's content as of the last confirmed sync (ingestion or projection).",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R00T",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R00V",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Reconciliation Trigger**: If `fileHash !== ingestedHash`, an unwitnessed edit occurred outside the DB, triggering reconciliation.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R00V",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R00W",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**DB-to-File Changes**: No hash is needed for DB updates. Because DB writes are always witnessed, the system can mark the corresponding artifact as needing re-projection within the same transaction.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R00W",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R00X",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00Y",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00Z",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R012",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01A",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01J"
    ],
    "title": "## 2. The Universal Node-Link-Edge Lineage",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R00Y",
    "children": [],
    "text": "The core graph is built on a clean, fractal inheritance lineage. Every relationship is a fully addressable, first-class Document.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R00Y",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R00Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R00Z",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R010",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R011"
    ],
    "title": "### A. BaseNode (The Root)",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R010",
    "children": [],
    "text": "The abstract root of all addressable content (inherited by `BlockNode`, `ArtifactNode`, `FolderNode`). It explicitly owns an array of its intrinsic links.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R010",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R011",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R011",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```json\n{\n  \"@id\": \"BaseNode\",\n  \"@type\": \"Class\",\n  \"@abstract\": [],\n  \"links\": { \"@type\": \"Set\", \"@class\": \"BaseLink\" }\n}\n```",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R011",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R012",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R013",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R014",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R019"
    ],
    "title": "### B. BaseLink (Intrinsic Connections)",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R013",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R013",
    "children": [],
    "text": "An abstract class representing connections authored physically *inside* a source node (e.g., Markdown hyperlinks).",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R013",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R014",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R014",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R015",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R017"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R014",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R015",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R015",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R016"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R015",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R016",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R016",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Inheritance**: Inherits from `BaseNode`. (This means links themselves possess a `links` array, allowing arbitrary depth for provenance or comments).",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R016",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R017",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R017",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R018"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R017",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R018",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R018",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Implicit Source**: Because a `BaseLink` resides within the `BaseNode.links` array, the node holding the array is implicitly the source.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R018",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R019",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R019",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```json\n{\n  \"@id\": \"BaseLink\",\n  \"@type\": \"Class\",\n  \"@abstract\": [],\n  \"@inherits\": [\"BaseNode\"],\n  \"target\": \"BaseNode\",\n  \"predicate\": \"xsd:string\"\n}\n```",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R019",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R01A",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01B",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01C",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01H"
    ],
    "title": "### C. BaseEdge (Extrinsic Assertions)",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R01B",
    "children": [],
    "text": "An abstract class representing independent semantic claims asserted from the outside (e.g., an AI Agent deducing a relationship).",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R01B",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R01C",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01D",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01F"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R01C",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R01D",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01E"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R01D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R01E",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Inheritance**: Inherits from `BaseLink`.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R01E",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R01F",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01G"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R01F",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R01G",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Explicit Source**: Because it floats independently of any node's `links` array, it adds a `source` pointer to explicitly declare its origin.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R01G",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R01H",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```json\n{\n  \"@id\": \"BaseEdge\",\n  \"@type\": \"Class\",\n  \"@abstract\": [],\n  \"@inherits\": [\"BaseLink\"],\n  \"source\": \"BaseNode\"\n}\n```",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R01H",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R01J",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01K",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01M"
    ],
    "title": "### D. Assertion (The Concrete Extrinsic Edge)",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R01K",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`BaseEdge` is abstract, so it can never be instantiated directly — something concrete has to exist to actually write an extrinsic claim (`impacts`, `verifies`, `derived_from`, `affects`, ...). `Assertion` is that one generic leaf: it adds no fields of its own, just makes the `source`/`predicate`/`target` (+ inherited `links`) lineage instantiable.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R01K",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R01M",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```json\n{\n  \"@id\": \"Assertion\",\n  \"@type\": \"Class\",\n  \"@inherits\": [\"BaseEdge\"]\n}\n```",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R01M",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R01N",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01P",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01V"
    ],
    "title": "## 3. Universal Addressability & Ownership",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R01P",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01Q",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01S"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R01P",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R01Q",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01R"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R01Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R01R",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**No Subdocuments**: `BaseLink` and `BaseEdge` are standard TerminusDB Classes, *not* `@subdocument`s. Every relationship possesses a global `@id`, enabling graph reification (assertions about assertions).",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R01R",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R01S",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01T"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R01S",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R01T",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Author-Based Placement**: Extrinsic assertions (`BaseEdge`) are never embedded into the nodes they connect. They are stored in the branch or artifact owned by the **Asserter** (the author). This ensures that agents can assert claims about human-authored nodes without mutating the human's artifact.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R01T",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R01V",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01W",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01X"
    ],
    "title": "### A. Native Backlinks & Bidirectional Traversal",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R01W",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Because TerminusDB is built on RDF triples under the hood, it natively indexes all edges in both directions. This gives the architecture two massive graph superpowers without requiring any custom backlink tables:",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R01W",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R01X",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01Y",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R021"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R01X",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R01Y",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01Z",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R020"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R01Y",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R01Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R01Z",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Upward Breadcrumbs (Context Retrieval)**:\n   Because `BaseLink` is a fully addressable Document, it does not need a physical `parent` pointer. If a user addresses a leaf node directly (`BaseLink/123`), they can follow the breadcrumbs \"upward\" to find the parent context:",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R01Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R020",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R020",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```javascript\n   // What ParentNode has a 'links' property pointing to me?\n   WOQL.triple(\"v:ParentNode\", \"links\", \"BaseLink/123\")\n   ```",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R020",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R021",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R021",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R022",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R023",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R024"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R021",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R022",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R022",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Universal Backlink Tracing (Logseq/Roam style)**:\n   You can instantly query the entire graph for *anything* that points to a specific target node, regardless of the predicate or origin.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R022",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R023",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R023",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```javascript\n   // What nodes point to this block, and via what relationship?\n   WOQL.triple(\"v:SourceNode\", \"v:Predicate\", \"BlockNode/MyTargetBlock\")\n   ```",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R023",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R024",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R024",
    "children": [],
    "text": "This instantly returns every intrinsic `BaseLink`, extrinsic `BaseEdge`, or parent document that references the target, enabling ultra-fast, database-native backlink panels.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R024",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R025",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R025",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R026",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R027",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02G",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02M"
    ],
    "title": "## 4. The Infinite Block Tree (Node Typology)",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R026",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R026",
    "children": [],
    "text": "The graph topology models all content as an infinite fractal tree spanning across folders, files, and blocks. The rigid boundaries between structural layers are eliminated to form a single continuous tree.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R026",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R027",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R027",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R028",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R029",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02E",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02F"
    ],
    "title": "### A. FolderNode (The Structural Container)",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R028",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R028",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Inherits from `BaseNode`. Represents a directory in the filesystem, acting as a seamless bridge in the infinite tree.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R028",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R029",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R029",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02A",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02C"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R029",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R02A",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02B"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R02A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R02B",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**`README.md` Ingestion**: A separate `README.md` file is a legacy \"dumb folder\" workaround. The `README.md` is fully absorbed into the `FolderNode`. Its content populates the folder's `text` (abstract) and initial `children` blocks. The `README.md` is not exposed as a separate `ArtifactNode`.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R02B",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R02C",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02D"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R02C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R02D",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**`children`**: Contains other nested `FolderNode`s and `ArtifactNode`s, alongside the parsed block children from the `README.md`.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R02D",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R02E",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Identity**: a Snowflake-style generated id, same scheme as `BlockNode` (§1.A); `path` is a plain, mutable field, not part of the key (Appendix G).",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R02E",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R02F",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```json\n{\n  \"@id\": \"FolderNode\",\n  \"@type\": \"Class\",\n  \"@inherits\": [\"BaseNode\"],\n  \"title\": \"xsd:string\",\n  \"path\": \"xsd:string\",\n  \"text\": { \"@type\": \"Optional\", \"@class\": \"xsd:string\" },\n  \"children\": { \"@type\": \"List\", \"@class\": \"BaseNode\" }\n}\n```",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R02F",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R02G",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02H",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02J",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02K"
    ],
    "title": "### B. ArtifactNode (The Physical Anchor)",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R02H",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Represents the physical file on disk. It handles file metadata and holds a single pointer to the root of the block tree. Inherits from `BaseNode` — without this, no `BaseLink`/`BaseEdge` could target or originate from a whole file, contradicting §3's universal-addressability goal.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R02H",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R02J",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Identity**: Snowflake-generated, same as `FolderNode` above; `path` is a plain, mutable field, not the key (Appendix G). Gains `title`/`text` to match the folding philosophy (§5) uniformly across the whole fractal lineage: `title` is the filename, `text` is an abstract of the file's own content (naive fallback — first paragraph — until AI-driven summarization, §5 enhancement backlog, actually exists).",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R02J",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R02K",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```json\n{\n  \"@id\": \"ArtifactNode\",\n  \"@type\": \"Class\",\n  \"@inherits\": [\"BaseNode\"],\n  \"title\": \"xsd:string\",\n  \"path\": \"xsd:string\",\n  \"text\": { \"@type\": \"Optional\", \"@class\": \"xsd:string\" },\n  \"fileHash\": \"xsd:string\",\n  \"lastTrackedAt\": \"xsd:dateTime\",\n  \"ingestedHash\": { \"@type\": \"Optional\", \"@class\": \"xsd:string\" },\n  \"lastIngestedAt\": { \"@type\": \"Optional\", \"@class\": \"xsd:dateTime\" },\n  \"root\": { \"@type\": \"Optional\", \"@class\": \"BlockNode\" }\n}\n```",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R02K",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R02M",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02N",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02P",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R039"
    ],
    "title": "### C. BlockNode (The Fractal Atom)",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R02N",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Inherits from `BaseNode`. Every distinct piece of content is a `BlockNode`. The schema is driven by the philosophy of **Abstraction by Folding**: a block's children fold into its `text` (abstract), which folds into a `title`, which folds into a hidden `@id`.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R02N",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R02P",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02Q",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02Y",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R030",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R032"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R02P",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R02Q",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02R",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02S"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R02Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R02R",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**`title` (The Semantic Label)**: Used for wikilinks and graph queries.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R02R",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R02S",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02T",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02W"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R02S",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R02T",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02V"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R02T",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R02V",
    "children": [],
    "text": "For direct UI input: The author is prompted to provide a title.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R02V",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R02W",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02X"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R02W",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R02X",
    "children": [],
    "text": "For Markdown ingestion: The parser uses an AI agent to summarize the block into a title. If AI is unavailable, it falls back to the block ID.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R02X",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R02Y",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02Z"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R02Y",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R02Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R02Z",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**`text` (The Abstract/Body)**: The actual content shown in the current document.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R02Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R030",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R030",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R031"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R030",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R031",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R031",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**`children`**: An ordered `List` of child `BlockNode`s.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R031",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R032",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R032",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R033",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R034"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R032",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R033",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R033",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**`unfolded`**: A boolean flag representing the persistent view-state for UIs and Agents.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R033",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R034",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R034",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R035",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R037"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R034",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R035",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R035",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R036"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R035",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R036",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R036",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Human UI & Agent Interface**: When rendering to a screen or an AI prompt, the graph defaults to *folded* (`false`) to manage cognitive/token overload. Only the current block's `text` and the children's `title`s are shown. If this flag is `true`, the subtree auto-expands on load.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R036",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R037",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R037",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R038"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R037",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R038",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R038",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Artifact Projection**: When syncing to a physical `.md` file, the tree is ALWAYS 100% unfolded (writing the full document to disk). This flag is ignored.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R038",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R039",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R039",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```json\n{\n  \"@id\": \"BlockNode\",\n  \"@type\": \"Class\",\n  \"@inherits\": [\"BaseNode\"],\n  \"title\": \"xsd:string\",\n  \"text\": { \"@type\": \"Optional\", \"@class\": \"xsd:string\" },\n  \"children\": { \"@type\": \"List\", \"@class\": \"BlockNode\" },\n  \"unfolded\": { \"@type\": \"Optional\", \"@class\": \"xsd:boolean\" }\n}\n```",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R039",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R03A",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03B",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03C",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03N"
    ],
    "title": "## 5. The Folding Philosophy & Graph Traversal",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R03B",
    "children": [],
    "text": "The entire architecture is governed by the philosophy of **Abstraction by Folding**: an infinite subtree folds into an abstract (`text`), which folds into a semantic label (`title`), which folds into a hidden `@id`.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R03B",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R03C",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03D",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03E"
    ],
    "title": "### A. The Three Projection Modes",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R03D",
    "children": [],
    "text": "How this folded state is handled depends strictly on the interaction interface:",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R03D",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R03E",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03F",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03H",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03K"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R03E",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R03F",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03G"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R03F",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R03G",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Artifact Projection (File Syncing)**: When the system serializes a graph back to a physical `.md` file, the tree is ALWAYS 100% unfolded. The persistent `unfolded` state is ignored, as the physical file must contain the entire document body. For `FolderNode`s, the block children are serialized back out to the folder's `README.md`.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R03G",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R03H",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03J"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R03H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R03J",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Human UI (Phase 1 Web App)**: The UI is folded by default and traverses seamlessly across folder/file boundaries. Users see the `text` (abstract) of the current node (`FolderNode`, `ArtifactNode`, or `BlockNode`) and the abstracts of its direct children. Expanding a `FolderNode` reveals child files/folders and its own `README.md` blocks inline without context switching.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R03J",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R03K",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03M"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R03K",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R03M",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Agentic Interface (BFS Traversal)**: AI agents interact with the graph exactly like the Human UI to manage token limitations. They receive folded views and can navigate continuously from a workspace root `FolderNode` down to a deeply nested `BlockNode` using BFS tool calls to expand subtrees.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R03M",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R03N",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03P",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03Q"
    ],
    "title": "### B. Link Targeting & \"Hover Previews\"",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R03P",
    "children": [],
    "text": "We distinguish between **Intrinsic Links** (`BaseNode.links`) and **Extrinsic Edges** (`BaseEdge`):",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R03P",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R03Q",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03R",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03T",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03W",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03Y",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R045"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R03Q",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R03R",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03S"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R03R",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R03S",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Intrinsic Links (`links`)**: Links and metadata (tags, properties) authored directly inside the node. Stored in `BaseNode.links`.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R03S",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R03T",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03V"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R03T",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R03V",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Extrinsic Edges (`BaseEdge`)**: Independent assertions created by external authors/agents. They float independently (to avoid mutating the source node) and are discovered via WOQL queries.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R03V",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R03W",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03X"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R03W",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R03X",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**UI Display**: The UI displays non-inline metadata/properties from `links` and queried extrinsic `BaseEdge`s in dedicated reference panels. Inline links remain rendered naturally inside the `text` body.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R03X",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R03Y",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03Z",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R040"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R03Y",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R03Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R03Z",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**The Preview Mechanism**:",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R03Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R040",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R040",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R041",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R043"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R040",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R041",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R041",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R042"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R041",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R042",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R042",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Human UI**: Humans receive the preview interactively by **hovering** over a link or wikilink in the UI, popping up the target block's abstract (`text`).",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R042",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R043",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R043",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R044"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R043",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R044",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R044",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Agent Interface**: Agents receive the target block's abstract (`text`) embedded directly in the `links` list returned by the projection/tool call, providing instant preview context without requiring UI hover triggers.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R044",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R045",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R045",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R046"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPA73R045",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R046",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R046",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Manual Jump**: If the user or agent needs more context than the target's abstract, they manually \"jump\" to the target block to explore its children.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R046",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R047",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R047",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R048",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R049",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04B",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04D",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04F",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04H",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04K",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04Q"
    ],
    "title": "## Appendix: Design History & Rationale",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R048",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R048",
    "children": [],
    "text": "This section archives the original problems that necessitated this design.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R048",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R049",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R049",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04A"
    ],
    "title": "### A. The Positional Identity Flaw",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R04A",
    "children": [],
    "text": "In Phase 0, `BlockNode` IDs were positional (`doc1_block_1`). If an author inserted a paragraph at the top of a document, all subsequent blocks shifted their IDs. This silently broke or orphaned any semantic edges pointing to those blocks upon re-ingestion. Moving to **Content-Addressed Identity** resolves this — though content-addressing itself was later found to have its own problems and was superseded; see Appendix F.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R04A",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R04B",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04C"
    ],
    "title": "### B. The `xsd:string` Anti-Pattern",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R04C",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Initially, relationships defined `subjectId` and `objectId` as `xsd:string`. This treated relationships as flat text rather than true graph edges, destroying referential integrity. Introducing `BaseNode` as a polymorphic type target resolves this, forcing all edges to point to actual documents in the database.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R04C",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R04D",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04E"
    ],
    "title": "### C. The Rejection of Subdocuments",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R04E",
    "children": [],
    "text": "TerminusDB's `@subdocument` feature was initially considered for `BaseNode.links` to tightly couple intrinsic links to their parent. However, subdocuments lose their global `@id`. In Aperas, every entity—even a single parsed link or punctuation mark—must be universally addressable so that external agents can comment on or refute it. Thus, subdocuments were rejected, and `BaseLink` was promoted to a full Document class.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R04E",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R04F",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04G"
    ],
    "title": "### D. Resolving Provenance",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R04G",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Initially, `provenance` was modeled as a hardcoded string or dedicated context object on an edge. By making `BaseLink` inherit from `BaseNode`, every link gets its own `links` array. Provenance is now simply achieved by pushing a new `BaseLink` (e.g., `predicate: \"asserted_by\"`) into the parent link's array, unifying the ontology completely.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R04G",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R04H",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04J"
    ],
    "title": "### E. The Infinite Block Tree",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R04J",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Initially, the schema enforced a rigid structural hierarchy (`DocumentNode` -> `BlockNode`). However, this rigid \"solid\" paradigm was abandoned in favor of a fractal, Logseq-inspired block tree. `DocumentNode` was eliminated entirely, as a document is conceptually just a root `BlockNode`. Flattening the graph to Markdown is now handled cleanly via an `unfolded` flag in the projection layer.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R04J",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R04K",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04M",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04N",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04P"
    ],
    "title": "### F. Separating Identity from Content Fingerprint",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R04M",
    "children": [],
    "text": "The content-addressed scheme from Appendix A (`@id = hash(parent context + content)`) conflated two requirements that pull in opposite directions: identity needs to stay constant across edits and moves so external references don't break; a content fingerprint needs to change whenever content changes, for dedup and change-detection. A single content-derived hash cannot satisfy both. Concretely, it broke two ways: (1) two independently-authored blocks with coincidentally identical text collapsed onto the same `@id`, silently merging distinct entities and their assertions; (2) because the hash was computed bottom-up through the tree, any edit to a leaf changed the hash of every ancestor up to the artifact root, orphaning assertions on whole sections for a single-word edit anywhere beneath them.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R04M",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R04N",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Resolved by decoupling the two entirely: `@id` is now a Snowflake-style generated identifier, assigned once and fully independent of content (§1.A) — collision-avoidance is deterministic (timestamp + machine identity + sequence counter), not derived from what the node contains. The content fingerprint (§1.B) turned out not to need a recursive/structural hash at all.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R04N",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R04P",
    "children": [],
    "text": "A first attempt at §1.B proposed reusing the bottom-up construction from this section — a recursive, per-`BlockNode` `treeHash` — for three things: detecting the DB-ahead-of-file case (by comparing it against `fileHash`), scoping reconciliation to only the diverged subtrees, and cross-checking the identity-matcher's decisions. The first use rested on a category error: `fileHash` hashes a flat string and a tree fingerprint hashes a nested structure — outputs of different functions over different domains, never meaningfully comparable regardless of whether real drift exists. Once that's gone, the DB-ahead-of-file case is better solved by direct on-write signaling instead (§1.B), and the remaining two uses (reconciliation scoping, cross-check) didn't justify a persisted, per-edit-maintained field on their own — reconciliation is rare and artifacts are bounded, human-document-sized trees, so a best-effort matcher can simply run over the whole tree each time without a hash-based pre-filter. Dropped entirely, not kept even as an on-demand technique — leaving two flat file-domain hashes (`fileHash`/`ingestedHash`) as the whole of the fingerprint design, and reconciliation itself resolved at the strategy level as best-effort content matching over the whole tree, with the specific matching algorithm left as an implementation detail.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R04P",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R04Q",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04R",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04S",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04T",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04V"
    ],
    "title": "### G. Separating Artifact/Folder Identity from Location",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R04R",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`ArtifactNode` and `FolderNode` were originally Lexical-keyed on `path` — not a deliberated design decision, just the obvious, simple choice made in an early, undesigned prototyping pass, before this document's identity/fingerprint rigor (§1, Appendix F) existed at all.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R04R",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R04S",
    "children": [],
    "text": "On inspection, while designing reconciliation matching (see `Aperas-reconciliation-matching-design.md`), this turned out to be the same category error Appendix F already fixed once for `BlockNode`, just on a different axis: identity conflated with a mutable property. There, the mutable property was content; here, it's location. A file or folder rename is a routine edit, exactly like a paragraph edit, not an identity change — but `path`-as-`@id` makes every rename destructive by construction, since the `@id` is *recomputed* from the new path, orphaning the old document's identity and everything that ever referenced it directly. The only way to route around that self-inflicted damage is to detect the rename after the fact and manually transplant `root` onto a freshly-identified document — real, working, but entirely unnecessary machinery, built to compensate for the identity scheme rather than because the problem demanded it.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R04S",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R04T",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Resolved the same way as Appendix F: `ArtifactNode` and `FolderNode` both get a Snowflake-generated identity (§1.A), and `path` becomes an ordinary mutable field. A detected rename (matched by content, same as everything else — see §4.A/B's `title`/`text` and the reconciliation doc's file/folder-matching design) becomes a field update on the same document, not a new identity; anything that referenced the artifact or folder by id keeps working with no transplant needed. `root` only ever needed transplanting because the container around it couldn't survive a move — fix the container, and the transplant machinery becomes unnecessary for this case (still needed for the case where a match genuinely fails and a new identity is warranted).",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R04T",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPA73R04V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPA73R04V",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Two costs were weighed before committing to this: losing the free, deterministic `id`-from-`path` lookup, and losing the database-enforced guarantee that no two documents can claim the same path. The first turned out not to be a cost at all — benchmarked, a `path`-filtered query came back faster than the direct id lookup it would replace (~7.5ms vs ~48ms at 50 documents). The second is real in shape (an application-level check-then-upsert race could in principle create duplicate `path`s) but not practically significant given how this project is actually deployed — one local TerminusDB per machine, reconciled via fetch/push, not a single server multiple machines write into concurrently; worth remembering if that deployment model ever changes.",
    "title": "00C5FPA73R04V",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAA10000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAA10000",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAA10001"
    ],
    "title": "Document Root",
    "type": "root",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAA10001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAA10001",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAA10002"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C64YWX58001",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
