  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF000R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF000R",
    "children": [],
    "text": "IDs & content fingerprint — **implemented and live-verified** (`Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §1). `web/src/lib/snowflake.ts` generates the 64-bit Snowflake-style identifier (timestamp + machine identity w/ personal failover + sequence counter, 13-char Crockford Base32); `astParser.ts` uses it for every `blockId` instead of the old content hash. `ArtifactNode.contentHash` renamed to `fileHash` throughout (`artifacts.ts`, `schema.json`) to match §1.B's file-domain-only fingerprint — no structural/recursive hash. Verified live: cleared stale pre-redesign `ArtifactNode`/`BlockNode` docs, ran `kg:track`+`kg:ingest` across all 8 artifacts (1144 blocks total, including a 648-block single-artifact burst), zero id collisions. Also found and fixed a real pre-existing bug while verifying: `getArtifactRecord` treated a missing document's raw 404 response (a string, not a thrown error) as a valid record, so untracked artifacts silently reported \"unchanged\" instead of erroring. Reconciliation (best-effort content matching, §1.C history in Appendix F) remains unimplemented — no code needed it yet, since ingestion so far has only ever run against uningested artifacts.",
    "title": "00C5FQW6CR015",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF000S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF000S",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FQW6CR016",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF000T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF000T",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Ingestion (`astParser.ts` and `artifacts.ts`) now parses Markdown into a deeply nested tree structure and commits the entire fractal tree via `ArtifactNode.root` in a single TerminusDB operation. Note: a plain `getDocument` read only ever returns `root`/`children` as reference ids, not the nested tree, so full-tree reads go through `getArtifactTreeViaGraphQL` (`graphql.ts`) instead — deliberately, not because the Document API is incapable of it (see `Aperas-architecture.md` §2's \"Read-path note\" for the full investigation, including a filed upstream bug, [terminusdb/terminusdb#2512](https://github.com/terminusdb/terminusdb/issues/2512)).",
    "title": "00C5FQW6CR017",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF000V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF000V",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FQW6CR018",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF000W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF000W",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`FolderNode` — **implemented and live-verified** (`Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §4.A). `web/src/lib/folders.ts` walks `AperasKG/artifacts/`, builds one `FolderNode` per directory, absorbs each directory's own `README.md` (parsed blocks become the folder's children; the file itself is never exposed as a separate `ArtifactNode`), and references nested `FolderNode`s/`ArtifactNode`s by id. Wired into `npm run kg:ingest`, which now rebuilds the whole folder tree in the same run as artifact ingestion. Added one concrete `Assertion` class (inherits the previously-uninstantiable abstract `BaseEdge`) to `schema.json`, needed to let `crud.ts`/`woql.ts` actually write/query extrinsic edges — documented in `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §2.D. **As-built today, both `FolderNode` and `ArtifactNode` are still Lexical-keyed on `path`** — the design has since moved to Snowflake ids for both (§4.A/§4.B, Appendix G), but that change isn't implemented yet; tracked under \"Reconciliation matching for re-ingestion\" below, since it's a prerequisite for that work, not this one.",
    "title": "00C5FPAHF000W",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-29T01:19:00.916Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF000X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF000X",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FQW6CR01A",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF000Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF000Y",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`crud.ts`/`woql.ts`/`graphql.ts`/`verifyPhase0.ts` — **migrated off the dead pre-redesign schema and live-verified**. `crud.ts` now provides `insertAssertion`/`deleteAssertionsInvolvingNode` for the new `Assertion` type; `woql.ts` queries `Assertion.source`/`predicate`/`target` (node-typed, not the old flat `xsd:string` `subjectId`/`objectId`) in both directions plus one-hop impact propagation; `graphql.ts` replaced the removed `docId`-scoped block query with `getArtifactTreeViaGraphQL` (bounded-depth nested `root`/`children` selection — GraphQL has no native recursion, so depth is generated explicitly, default 10). `verifyPhase0.ts` was rewritten into a full idempotent, self-cleaning live test of the whole pipeline (AST parsing → track/ingest → GraphQL tree read → `FolderNode` ingestion → `Assertion` CRUD + WOQL traversal → temporal commit management); `npm run verify:phase0 -- --db` and `npm run build` both confirmed passing.",
    "title": "00C5FQW6CR01B",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF000Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF000Z",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FQW6CR01C",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF0010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF0010",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Discovered while wiring this up**: TerminusDB enforces referential integrity on document delete — deleting a still-referenced document (e.g. an `ArtifactNode` still listed in a `FolderNode.children`, or a `BlockNode` still pointed to by `ArtifactNode.root`) fails with a `SchemaCheckFailure`, not silently. The best-effort delete helpers in `crud.ts` (`deleteDocumentIfExists`/`deleteDocumentsIfExist`) used to swallow *all* errors on the assumption only \"not found\" could occur — that assumption was wrong and masked this failure mode; they now log instead of swallowing silently, and any caller managing referenced state (like `verifyPhase0.ts`'s cleanup) has to delete in reverse-reference order.",
    "title": "00C5FQW6CR01D",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
