  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF0015",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF0015",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Heading levels don't define tree structure**: `astParser.ts`'s `isStructural` check treats `heading` like any other flat block type, so a document's headings and their following paragraphs/lists all end up as siblings directly under the root, with no nesting by heading level. Confirmed live: a doc with `# Title` / `## Section A` / `## Section B` parses into `Title, (intro), Section A, (para), (list), Section B, ...` all as flat children of \"Document Root,\" not `Title → Section A → (para), (list)`. Lists themselves (ordered and unordered) do nest correctly — `list → listItem → nested list → ...` — this gap is specific to headings. **Must ship before reconciliation matching** (below) goes live — see that entry for why.",
    "title": "00C5FPAHF0015",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-29T01:19:00.916Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF0016",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF0016",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT001B"
    ],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB0019",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF0017",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF0017",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Reconciliation matching for re-ingestion** — **design settled, not yet implemented** (`Aperas-reconciliation-matching-design.md`, `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §1.B/§4.A/§4.B/Appendix G): re-ingesting an already-ingested artifact currently still orphans its entire previous `BlockNode` tree. Design: Gestalt (Ratcliff/Obershelp) tree diff, leaf content anchors containers by context, explicit `tombstonedAt` marker for unmatched nodes (not implicit), covers `FolderNode`/`ArtifactNode` structural drift as well as within-artifact `BlockNode` content, reports changed/moved as well as added/removed. Surfaced a prerequisite schema fix along the way: `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode` move off `Lexical` keying on `path` to Snowflake ids (same as `BlockNode`), `path` becoming a plain mutable field — full rationale in Appendix G. **Blocked on**: heading-nesting (below) must ship first, or the first re-ingest after that fix mass-orphans everything reconciliation was meant to protect.",
    "title": "00C5FPAHF0017",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-29T01:19:00.916Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF0018",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF0018",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT001D"
    ],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB001B",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF0019",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF0019",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Fractal Ontology Enhancements** (`Aperas-fractal-ontology-implementation-plan.md` Stage 2, items 4-5): AI-driven summarization during ingestion (splitting blocks intelligently into `title` vs `text`) and structural extraction of inline Markdown links into `BaseLink` edges. Confirmed still unimplemented: `astParser.ts`'s `isStructural` node-type list doesn't even include `link`, so inline Markdown links are currently just silently absorbed into the parent block's raw `text`, not extracted at all.",
    "title": "00C5FQW6D0004",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF001A",
