    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF001E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF001E",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FPAHF001E",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-29T01:19:00.916Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF001F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF001F",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Reconciling separate hosts' diverged `aperas_apeiron` histories (push/pull, possibly rebase) — currently only fetched-and-inspected, not merged.",
    "title": "00C5FPAHF001F",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-29T01:19:00.916Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF001G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF001G",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF0012",
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT001Y"
    ],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB800A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF001H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF001H",
    "children": [],
    "title": "## Appendix: cross-store `bundle`/`unbundle` incompatibility investigation",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF001J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF001J",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FQW6D000D",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF001K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF001K",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FQW6D000E",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF001M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF001M",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Historical record — the `restore.sh`/`bundle` workflow this investigation covers predates its relocation to `Aperas/scripts/` (see \"KG backup/restore\" above); kept for reference in case a similar mechanism is reintroduced.",
    "title": "00C5FQW6D000F",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF001N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF001N",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FQW6D000G",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF001P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF001P",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Symptom: `aperas_apeiron_snapshot_A.bundle` (made on Host A) and `aperas_apeiron_snapshot_B.bundle` (made on Host B) each verify cleanly **only on their own origin machine**, and fail deterministically with `error(unknown_layer_reference(<hash>))` on the other — a different specific missing-layer hash each time.",
    "title": "00C5FQW6D000H",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF001Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF001Q",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FQW6D000J",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF001R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF001R",
    "children": [],
    "text": "An earlier pass at this investigation, run on a single host in isolation, found a byte pattern in a snapshot that looked like Latin-1/UTF-8 mojibake corruption (reversing it produced a plausible gzip header) and concluded the file was corrupted. **That conclusion was wrong and has been retracted** — the same file was later shown to unbundle perfectly on its own origin host, which a genuinely corrupted file cannot do. The byte pattern was a coincidental artifact, not evidence of corruption.",
    "title": "00C5FQW6D000K",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF001S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF001S",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FQW6D000M",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF001T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF001T",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Ruled out version mismatch: both machines confirmed running byte-identical `TerminusDB v12.0.7 (57f2093baeafd65e16004e84b7b58e0c5cf72858)` / `terminusdb-store v0.19.8`.",
    "title": "00C5FQW6D000N",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF001V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF001V",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FQW6D000P",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF001W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF001W",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Ruled out the `auto-optimize` community plugin (`/plugins/auto-optimize.pl`, a probabilistic post-commit layer squash/GC): disabled on both machines (moved the plugin file out, restarted), re-tested with a brand-new minimal scratch database — still failed cross-host identically.",
    "title": "00C5FQW6D000Q",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF001X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF001X",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FQW6D000R",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF001Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF001Y",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Ruled out store \"age\": reproduced with a store `store init`'d seconds before the test, same as the destination.",
    "title": "00C5FQW6D000S",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF001Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF001Z",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FQW6D000T",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF0020",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF0020",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Decisive isolation, no second machine needed**: ran two independent TerminusDB containers (`terminusdb` and a throwaway `terminusdb-freshtest`, same image, same physical host, plugin off on both) and bundled/unbundled between them. Same failure. A positive control — unbundling the same file back into a *different database within its own originating container* — succeeded every time. This isolates the variable precisely: **it's not host A vs. host B, or even separate machines at all — it's any two independent TerminusDB stores (server instances/storage directories), even side-by-side on one host.**",
    "title": "00C5FQW6D000V",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF0021",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF0021",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FQW6D000W",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF0022",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF0022",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Cross-checked against prior art: [terminusdb/terminusdb#1147](https://github.com/terminusdb/terminusdb/issues/1147) reports the identical symptom moving a bundle between two instances, never reproduced by the maintainer, closed stale/not-planned. [terminusdb/terminusdb#1235](https://github.com/terminusdb/terminusdb/pull/1235) (\"an initial effort to figure out #1147 without success\") added CLI bundle/unbundle tests that call `store.init()` exactly once and share that one store across every test — so its test suite never actually exercises the cross-store case, which is the one that fails.",
    "title": "00C5FQW6D000X",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF0023",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF0023",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FQW6D000Y",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF0024",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF0024",
    "children": [],
    "text": "The official [\"move a database between servers\" backup/restore guide](https://terminusdb.org/docs/enterprise-backup-restore/) is scoped to **Enterprise edition** (different mechanism: `/api/bundle` + `/api/unbundle` REST endpoints, target pre-created) — not a documented guarantee for the Community-edition CLI commands we're using.",
    "title": "00C5FQW6D000Z",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF0025",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF0025",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FQW6D0010",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF0026",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF0026",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Filed as [terminusdb/terminusdb#2509](https://github.com/terminusdb/terminusdb/issues/2509), including the two-store repro and a note about the test-coverage gap in #1235. Draft/record kept at `terminusdb-issue-bundle-cross-store.md`.",
    "title": "00C5FQW6D0011",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF0027",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF0027",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FQW6D0012",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF0028",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF0028",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Conclusion for this project: `bundle`/`unbundle`/`restore.sh` remain valid for same-store snapshot/rollback, but are not to be relied on for cross-machine transfer.",
    "title": "00C5FQW6D0013",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAG000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAG000",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR000"
    ],
    "title": "Document Root",
    "type": "root",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR000",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR001",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR002",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR003",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR009"
    ],
    "title": "# The Aperas Extensibility Model: Apeiron to Perata",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR001",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Aperas is not a monolithic application with a single, closed database; it is an engine for growing forms (Perata) out of a formless core (Apeiron).",
    "title": "00C5FPAKAR001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR002",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Because there will be many different Domain KGs (e.g., `ArchitectureKG`, `PersonalKG`, `ProjectX_KG`), the boundary between the Core and the Domain must support deep **extension and refinability**.",
    "title": "00C5FPAKAR002",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR003",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR004"
    ],
    "title": "## 1. Core vs. Community Governance",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR004",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR005",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR007"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAKAR004",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR005",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR006"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAKAR005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR006",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Aperas (The Apeiron Core):** Managed by the Core Dev Team. It provides the universal potential: the database driver, the base universal schemas (`BaseNode`, `BaseLink`, `BaseEdge`, `BlockNode`, `ArtifactNode`), and the infrastructure tooling (like `restore.sh`).",
    "title": "00C5FPAKAR006",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR007",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR008"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAKAR007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR008",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**A Domain KG (The Perata):** Managed by the Community. A specific KG repository (like `AperasKG`) is a specific materialization. It contains the raw content (`artifacts/`), **and** the specific logic that defines its shape (its Schemas, Ontologies, and Transducers).",
    "title": "00C5FPAKAR008",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR009",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00A",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00B",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00J",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00T"
    ],
    "title": "## 2. Mechanisms of Extension (OOP & Composition)",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR00A",
    "children": [],
    "text": "The technical implementation of this extensibility leverages Object-Oriented polymorphism in TerminusDB and functional composition in TypeScript.",
    "title": "00C5FPAKAR00A",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR00B",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00C",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00D"
    ],
    "title": "### A. Schema Extension (`@inherits`)",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR00C",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Domain KGs can define custom node shapes that natively inherit properties from the Aperas Core nodes using the `@inherits` JSON-LD keyword.",
    "title": "00C5FPAKAR00C",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR00D",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00E",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00G"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAKAR00D",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR00E",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00F"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAKAR00E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR00F",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Property Inheritance**: A domain `RequirementNode` inheriting from `BlockNode` automatically gains `title`, `text`, and `children`, plus its own specific fields like `priority`.",
    "title": "00C5FPAKAR00F",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR00G",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00H"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAKAR00G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR00H",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Subsumption (Polymorphism)**: TerminusDB natively understands this inheritance Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG). A query for `BlockNode` will automatically return all `RequirementNode` instances. *(See the official [TerminusDB Schema Reference Guide](https://terminusdb.org/docs/schema-reference-guide/#inherits) for details).*",
    "title": "00C5FPAKAR00H",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR00J",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00K",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00M",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00N"
    ],
    "title": "### B. Ontology Extension (Edge Subclassing)",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR00K",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Aperas adopts **Edge Subclassing (OOP)** for defining predicates and relationships. \nInstead of relying on fragile string fields, relationships are modeled as abstract schema classes (e.g., `BaseEdge`). A Domain KG can define specific relationships that inherit from these bases:",
    "title": "00C5FPAKAR00K",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR00M",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```json\n{ \"@id\": \"AffectsEdge\", \"@type\": \"Class\", \"@inherits\": [\"BaseEdge\"], \"source\": \"BlockNode\", \"target\": \"BlockNode\" }\n{ \"@id\": \"BlocksEdge\", \"@type\": \"Class\", \"@inherits\": [\"AffectsEdge\"] }\n```",
    "title": "00C5FPAKAR00M",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR00N",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00P"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAKAR00N",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR00P",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00Q",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00R",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00S"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAKAR00P",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR00Q",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**WOQL Subsumption Query**: Because the edge is an object in a hierarchy, you query it using `isa()`, which natively understands subsumption. *(See the [WOQL Class Reference Guide](https://terminusdb.org/docs/woql-class-reference-guide/#is-a) for details on `isa`)*.",
    "title": "00C5FPAKAR00Q",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR00R",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```javascript\n    WOQL.isa(\"v:EdgeId\", \"AffectsEdge\")\n        .triple(\"v:EdgeId\", \"source\", \"v:NodeA\")\n        .triple(\"v:EdgeId\", \"target\", \"v:NodeB\")\n    ```",
    "title": "00C5FPAKAR00R",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR00S",
    "children": [],
    "text": "This single query automatically fetches all `AffectsEdge` instances **and** all domain-specific `BlocksEdge` instances seamlessly, with strict typing constraints.",
    "title": "00C5FPAKAR00S",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR00T",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00V",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00W"
    ],
    "title": "### C. Transducer Extension (Pipeline & Class Overrides)",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR00V",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Because transducers are TypeScript logic, they extend via standard programming patterns:",
    "title": "00C5FPAKAR00V",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR00W",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00X",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00Z"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAKAR00W",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR00X",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00Y"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAKAR00X",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR00Y",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Pipeline Composition**: Using tools like `unified.js`, the core provides a base pipeline (`unified().use(remarkParse)`). A Domain KG injects its own specific plugins (`.use(domainSpecificYamlPlugin)`) into the chain.",
    "title": "00C5FPAKAR00Y",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR00Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR00Z",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR010"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAKAR00Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAKAR010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAKAR010",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**OOP Class Inheritance**: A domain script can extend a core parser class (`class ArchitectureTransducer extends BaseMarkdownTransducer`) to override specific parsing behaviors.",
    "title": "00C5FPAKAR010",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ0000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ0000",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ8000"
    ],
    "title": "Document Root",
    "type": "root",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ8000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ8000",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ8001",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ8002",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800X",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ801A"
    ],
    "title": "# Aperas Fractal Ontology - Implementation Plan",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ8001",
    "children": [],
    "text": "This plan outlines the steps to refactor the Aperas Knowledge Graph codebase to implement the fractal block-tree ontology designed in `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md`. Stage 1 is fully implemented and live-verified; Stage 2 is implemented except items 4 (Link Extraction) and 5 (Title vs. Text Split), which remain open; Stage 3 (Database & UI Alignment) hasn't started. See `Aperas-dev-status.md` for current status and `Aperas-architecture.md` for the as-built reference. Node identity evolved past what Stage 2 anticipated (content-addressed hashing was tried and superseded by Snowflake-style ids — see `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` Appendix F); this plan is kept as a historical record, not a live checklist.",
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ8001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ8002",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ8003",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ8004"
    ],
    "title": "## Stage 1: Core Schema Overhaul",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ8003",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Target Files**: Create `web/src/lib/schema.json` and delete `web/src/lib/schema.ts`",
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ8003",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ8004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ8004",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ8005",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ8007",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ8009",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800B",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800M"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ8004",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ8005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ8005",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ8006"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ8005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ8006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ8006",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Eliminate `schema.ts`**: The current `schema.ts` file contains useless TypeScript interfaces that type the TerminusDB schema metadata (e.g., `docId: \"xsd:string\"`). This is a double-maintenance anti-pattern. We will delete `schema.ts` entirely.",
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ8006",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ8007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ8007",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ8008"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ8007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ8008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ8008",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Create `schema.json`**: Create a pure, static JSON array file representing the raw JSON-LD schema required by TerminusDB.",
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ8008",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ8009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ8009",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800A"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ8009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ800A",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Clean Slate**: Do not port over the legacy `DocumentNode`, `SpanNode`, or `TripleAssertion` definitions to the new JSON file.",
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ800A",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ800B",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800C",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800D"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ800B",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ800C",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Implement Lineage (in `schema.json`)**:",
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ800C",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ800D",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800E",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800G",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800J"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ800D",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ800E",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800F"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ800E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ800F",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Define `BaseNode` (Abstract class, `links: Set<BaseLink>`).",
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ800F",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ800G",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800H"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ800G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ800H",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Define `BaseLink` (Inherits `BaseNode`, adds `target: BaseNode`).",
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ800H",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ800J",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800K"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ800J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ800K",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Define `BaseEdge` (Inherits `BaseLink`, adds `source: BaseNode`).",
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ800K",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ800M",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800N",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800P"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ800M",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ800N",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Implement Topology (in `schema.json`)**:",
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ800N",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ800P",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800Q",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800S",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800V"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ800P",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ800Q",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800R"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ800Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ800R",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Define `FolderNode` (Inherits `BaseNode`, adds `title`, `path`, `text`, `children: List<BaseNode>`).",
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ800R",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ800S",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800T"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ800S",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ800T",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Define `BlockNode` (Inherits `BaseNode`, adds `title`, `text`, `children: List<BlockNode>`, `unfolded: boolean`).",
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ800T",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ800V",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800W"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ800V",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ800W",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Define `ArtifactNode` (adds `path`, `contentHash`, `root: BlockNode`).",
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ800W",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ800X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
