      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ801Q"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ801G",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ801H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ801H",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ801J"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ801H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ801J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ801J",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Update WOQL/GraphQL queries to support BFS traversal seamlessly across `FolderNode`, `ArtifactNode`, and `BlockNode` boundaries.",
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ801J",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ801K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ801K",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ801M"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ801K",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ801M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ801M",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Stub or update the Markdown generation logic to respect the `unfolded` property and serialize `FolderNode` block children back into `README.md`s.",
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ801M",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ801N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ801N",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ801P"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ801N",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ801P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ801P",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Update SolidJS UI tree components to render the polymorphic hierarchy smoothly (Folder -> File -> Block).",
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ801P",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ801Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ801Q",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ801R"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ801Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAMJ801R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAMJ801R",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Prepare UI components to handle the \"Hover Preview\" of link targets.",
    "title": "00C5FPAMJ801R",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G000",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G001"
    ],
    "title": "Document Root",
    "type": "root",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G001",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G002",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G003",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00B",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00D",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00K",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00N",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00R",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00Y"
    ],
    "title": "# Reconciliation Matching — Design",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G002",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Re-ingesting an already-ingested artifact today just orphans its entire prior `BlockNode` tree. The strategy for doing better was settled in `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §1.B and Appendix F; this doc works out the algorithm that actually does it. The design below is settled; nothing has been implemented yet.",
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G002",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G003",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G004"
    ],
    "title": "## Settled already (prior to this doc)",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G004",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G005",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G007",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G009"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G004",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G005",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G006"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G006",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Reconciliation fires when `fileHash !== ingestedHash` — an edit landed on disk outside the DB (§1.B).",
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G006",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G007",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G008"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G008",
    "children": [],
    "text": "The approach is best-effort content matching over the whole tree, not a positional or hash-prefiltered pass — artifacts are bounded, human-document-sized trees, so there's no need to scope the search first (Appendix F).",
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G008",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G009",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00A"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G00A",
    "children": [],
    "text": "A persisted, per-edit-maintained structural hash (`treeHash`) was considered and explicitly dropped, for both identity and reconciliation-scoping purposes (Appendix F).",
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G00A",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G00B",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00C"
    ],
    "title": "## Blocking prerequisite: heading nesting must ship first",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G00C",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`astParser.ts` currently treats `heading` as a flat block type — a document's headings and their following content all end up as siblings under the root, with no nesting by heading level (tracked in `Aperas-dev-status.md`). This has to be fixed *before* reconciliation goes live, not after: if reconciliation ships against today's flat shape and the heading fix lands later, every existing document reshapes at once (every block's parent changes), and the matcher will read that as \"everything changed,\" orphaning the whole graph in one re-ingest — precisely the outcome reconciliation exists to prevent. Lists (ordered and unordered) already nest correctly and aren't affected.",
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G00C",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G00D",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00E",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00F",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00G",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00H",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00J"
    ],
    "title": "## 1. The matching algorithm: Gestalt, not Myers",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G00E",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Chosen deliberately over Myers/LCS-style diffing: Myers optimizes for the fewest edit operations (a machine-optimal cost function); Gestalt Pattern Matching (Ratcliff/Obershelp — the algorithm behind Python's `difflib.SequenceMatcher`) finds the longest matching contiguous run first, then recurses on the remainder either side of it. The two produce different notions of \"correct\" — Myers can produce confusing criss-cross matches around repeated content (the same reason git offers `--patience`/`--histogram` as alternatives to its default Myers diff), where what matters for reconciliation isn't a compact edit script, it's whether the match a human would recognize as \"the same block, edited\" is the one preserved. Natural-over-optimal is the right cost function here, since the actual consequence of a match is whether a `BaseLink`/`Assertion` stays attached to what a person would agree is the same content.",
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G00E",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G00F",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Applied recursively, level by level: the root is always trivially matched (one root per `ArtifactNode`); for any matched parent pair, their `children` lists are diffed in two stages, then each matched child pair recurses into its own children.",
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G00F",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G00G",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Stage A — anchor on leaf content.** Filter each level's children down to content-bearing nodes (`heading`, `paragraph`, `code`) and run Gestalt on that subsequence. The comparison key is **heading XOR text**: a heading's own line when the node is a heading, its own `text` otherwise — never the placeholder `title` a non-heading block currently carries (which is just its own `blockId`, and would always differ between old and new by construction, silently defeating any matcher that touched it).",
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G00G",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G00H",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Stage B — anchor containers by context, not content.** Container-type nodes (`list`, `listItem`, `blockquote`) carry no reliable content of their own to compare (see the container-text gap below) — and don't need to. Their meaning comes from what's written around them (\"...with the following list:\", \"The quote above is...\"), so the leaf matches from Stage A partition both children lists into segments (before the first anchor, between each consecutive anchor pair, after the last); within a segment, containers align to their counterpart by type and relative position. No subtree signature, no hash, transient or otherwise — the surrounding matched prose is the anchor.",
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G00H",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G00J",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Gap to close alongside this**: `list`/`listItem` currently store the *entire subtree's* raw slice as their own `text` — confirmed live, e.g. a `listItem`'s `text` byte-for-byte duplicated one level down in its own paragraph child. Container-type nodes should carry no own `text` at all; content lives only in their leaf descendants. This is what makes Stage B's \"containers have no content to compare\" true by design rather than by omission.",
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G00J",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G00K",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00M"
    ],
    "title": "## 2. Duplicate/ambiguous leaves: let it go",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G00M",
    "children": [],
    "text": "If two leaf blocks with identical content can't be told apart by context (unanchored by anything on either side, the \"two Notes blocks\" case), decline to match rather than guess. Both old candidates get tombstoned, the new one mints a fresh id. Precision over recall — a wrong guess silently misattributes whatever pointed at the old block to its content-twin; declining just means the tombstone stands unresolved, which is visible and inspectable rather than silently wrong.",
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G00M",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G00N",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00P",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00Q"
    ],
    "title": "## 3. Fate of unmatched old blocks: explicit tombstone",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G00P",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Not implicit (a document that just stops being referenced carries no signal it was ever a deliberate removal, versus an orphan-by-bug, versus mid-reconciliation limbo — that's not a weaker tombstone, it isn't one at all). An explicit `tombstonedAt` field, set when a node is determined to have no match: removed from whatever `children`/`root` list held it, but the document persists at its own `@id` — any edge still resolves, and can render \"removed on `<date>`\" instead of either dangling silently or reattaching to the wrong thing.",
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G00P",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G00Q",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Applies uniformly across `BlockNode`, `ArtifactNode`, and `FolderNode` (see §4).",
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G00Q",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G00R",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00S",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00T",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00V",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00W",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00X"
    ],
    "title": "## 4. Scope: the whole infinite tree, and a prerequisite identity fix",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G00S",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Reconciliation covers `FolderNode`/`ArtifactNode` structural drift too, not just within-artifact `BlockNode` content — a file renamed or moved on disk is the same kind of event as a block moved to a different section, and gets the same treatment.",
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G00S",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G00T",
    "children": [],
    "text": "This surfaced a real prerequisite: `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode` were Lexical-keyed on `path`, an undesigned choice from an early prototyping pass, not a deliberated one. That's the same category error Appendix F already fixed once for `BlockNode` — identity conflated with a mutable property, content there, location here — and it means a rename is destructive by construction (the `@id` is recomputed from the new path, so the old identity, and everything that referenced it, breaks). **Resolved**: `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode` get Snowflake-generated ids like `BlockNode`; `path` becomes an ordinary mutable field. A detected rename becomes a field update on the existing document, not a new identity — no tombstone-and-transplant needed for the artifact/folder itself (only `root`/tree-content ever needed transplanting, and only because the container around it couldn't survive a move under the old scheme). Full rationale in `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` Appendix G.",
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G00T",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G00V",
    "children": [],
    "text": "This also means `ArtifactNode` needs `title`/`text` fields it didn't have before — the folding philosophy (§5) applied uniformly: full dir tree → README → abstract (`text`, first paragraph as a naive stand-in until real AI summarization exists) → filename (`title`).",
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G00V",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G00W",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Matching rule for files/folders — title first, abstract as fallback, not \"never trust the name.\"** Unlike a non-heading block's placeholder title (always meaningless, always differs), a filename is a real, human-authored, sticky signal — the same category as a heading's own text. So: match unchanged paths trivially (already free — `path` is a plain field now, so an unchanged path is an exact match with no reconciliation logic needed at all). For the leftover set only (an old path gone from disk, a new file with no tracked `ArtifactNode`), fall back to matching by `text` (abstract) similarity to detect a genuine rename — same \"let it go if ambiguous\" rule as leaf blocks. A rename is a real, deliberate edit (like changing a heading), not something to be blind to by default; it should just take a radical-enough change in the abstract to actually get missed.",
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G00W",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G00X",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Cost check before committing: a `path`-filtered query replacing today's free direct-id lookup benchmarked *faster* (~7.5ms vs ~48ms at 50 documents) — not a cost at all. Losing the database-enforced path-uniqueness guarantee is real in shape (an application-level check-then-upsert race could in principle create duplicate paths) but not practically significant given this project's actual deployment — one local TerminusDB per machine, reconciled via fetch/push, not concurrent writers against a shared server.",
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G00X",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G00Y",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00Z",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G010",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G019"
    ],
    "title": "## 5. Visibility: report changed and moved, not just added/removed",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G00Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G00Z",
    "children": [],
    "text": "A wrong match is silent by nature — nothing errors, an edge just ends up pointing at different content than a human expects — so a reconciliation pass should produce a summary. Not just counts of added/removed: **changed** and **moved** are their own categories, and they're not separate machinery, they fall directly out of classifying each match's outcome, applied uniformly at every level of the fractal tree (`FolderNode`/`ArtifactNode`/`BlockNode`):",
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G00Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G010",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G011",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G013",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G015",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G017"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G010",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G011",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G011",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G012"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G011",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G012",
    "children": [],
    "text": "same content, same position/path → unchanged",
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G012",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G013",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G013",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G014"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G013",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G014",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G014",
    "children": [],
    "text": "same content, different position/path → **moved**",
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G014",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G015",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G015",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G016"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G015",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G016",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G016",
    "children": [],
    "text": "different content, same identity → **changed**",
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G016",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G017",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G017",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G018"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G017",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G018",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G018",
    "children": [],
    "text": "no match → added (new) or removed (tombstoned)",
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G018",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAP2G019",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAP2G019",
    "children": [],
    "text": "A renamed file is the `ArtifactNode`-level instance of the same operation as a block moved to a different section: an orphaned old path matched against an untracked new path by content similarity, one mechanism, three fractal layers.",
    "title": "00C5FPAP2G019",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE8000",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8001"
    ],
    "title": "Document Root",
    "type": "root",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE8001",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8002",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8003",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8004",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8007",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800J",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800W",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800Z",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE801E"
    ],
    "title": "# TerminusDB CLI Status Walkthrough & Operational Reference",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE8002",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Operational reference for checking status, commit logs, document contents, and remote state of the `aperas_apeiron` database using the `tdb` CLI shortcut. For complete reference of TerminusDB CLI, see the [official documentation](https://terminusdb.org/docs/terminusdb-cli-commands/).",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE8002",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE8003",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```bash\nalias tdb='docker exec terminusdb /app/terminusdb/terminusdb'\n```",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE8003",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE8004",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8005",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8006"
    ],
    "title": "## 1. Database & Branch Verification",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE8005",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Confirm database presence and inspect active branches across all stored databases:",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE8005",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE8006",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```bash\ntdb db list --branches\n```",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE8006",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE8007",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8008",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800B",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800E"
    ],
    "title": "## 2. Commit Log Inspection & Document Filtering",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE8008",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8009",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800A"
    ],
    "title": "### Standard Branch Log",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE8009",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Inspect full commit history for the main branch:",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE8009",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE800A",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```bash\ntdb log admin/aperas_apeiron | less\n```",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE800A",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE800B",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800C",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800D"
    ],
    "title": "### Compact Local-Time History",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE800C",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Use `tdb-log.sh` (located in `Aperas/scripts/`) for local-time formatting and auto-paging. Output defaults to 20 commits (`--count` parameter is only needed when overriding, e.g., `--count 50` or `--count -1`):",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE800C",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE800D",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```bash\nAperas/scripts/tdb-log.sh\n```",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE800D",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE800E",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800F",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800H"
    ],
    "title": "### Document History Filtering",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE800F",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800G"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAQE800F",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE800G",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Performance Warning**: `tdb history --id=\"...\"` is measurably slow — over 6× slower than dumping the entire log (572 commits: `log --count -1` ~2.2s vs. `history` for one document ~13s). It's not walking an index of changed ids per commit; the exact mechanism wasn't confirmed, but the timing is consistent with checking the document's actual state at every commit along the way. Use message-filtering on `tdb log` or `tdb-log.sh` as the fast alternative:",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE800G",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE800H",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```bash\n# Fast message filter via tdb-log.sh\nAperas/scripts/tdb-log.sh --filter \"Aperas-dev-status.md\"\n\n# Fast JSON filter via raw CLI & jq\ntdb log admin/aperas_apeiron --json --count -1 2>/dev/null \\\n  | jq '.[] | select(.message | contains(\"Aperas-dev-status.md\"))'\n```",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE800H",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE800J",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800K",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800M",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800S"
    ],
    "title": "## 3. Substrate Document Inspection",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE800K",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Retrieve stored documents by JSON-LD class (`ArtifactNode`, `BlockNode`, `BaseLink`, `BaseEdge`):",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE800K",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE800M",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800N",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800P",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800Q"
    ],
    "title": "### Raw JSONL Output",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE800N",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`tdb doc get` outputs raw JSONL (one JSON object per line) with UTC timestamps and literal `\\n`/`\\t` escape sequences:",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE800N",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE800P",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```bash\ntdb doc get admin/aperas_apeiron --type=\"ArtifactNode\" | jq | less\n```",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE800P",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE800Q",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800R"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAQE800Q",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE800R",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Note**: Add `--as-list=true` to convert JSONL lines into a single JSON array for program analysis.",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE800R",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE800S",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800T",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800V"
    ],
    "title": "### Unescaped Local-Time View (`tdb-doc.sh`)",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE800T",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Use `tdb-doc.sh` to unescape embedded line breaks into readable text and convert ISO UTC timestamps to local time:",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE800T",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE800V",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```bash\nAperas/scripts/tdb-doc.sh --type=\"BlockNode\"\n```",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE800V",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE800W",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800X",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800Y"
    ],
    "title": "## 4. Direct WOQL Graph Queries",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE800X",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Execute arbitrary WOQL queries against the substrate:",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE800X",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE800Y",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```bash\ntdb query admin/aperas_apeiron \"t(X, 'docId', Y)\" --json\n```",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE800Y",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE800Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE800Z",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8010",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8012",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8015",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8018",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE801B"
    ],
    "title": "## 5. SSH-Tunneled Remotes",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE8010",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8011"
    ],
    "title": "### Transport Overview",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8011",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE8011",
    "children": [],
    "text": "TerminusDB's native remote commands (`push`/`pull`/`fetch`/`clone`) communicate exclusively over HTTP(S) REST APIs without native SSH transport support. TerminusDB itself listens on `0.0.0.0:6363` inside the container — the loopback-only restriction (`127.0.0.1:6363`) is this project's own `docker run -p` configuration, not a TerminusDB default. Either way, cross-machine communication between separate hosts requires an SSH local port forward tunnel here.",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE8011",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE8012",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8013",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8014"
    ],
    "title": "### 1. Establish SSH Local Port Forwarding",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8013",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE8013",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Forward local port `6364` on the source host to port `6363` on the remote target host. Bind to `0.0.0.0` so the local Docker container network can reach the tunnel:",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE8013",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8014",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE8014",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```bash\nssh -N -f -L 0.0.0.0:6364:localhost:6363 <user>@<remote-host>\n```",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE8014",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8015",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE8015",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8016",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8017"
    ],
    "title": "### 2. Configure Host Firewall (UFW)",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8016",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE8016",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Allow traffic from the Docker bridge subnet (`172.17.0.0/16`) to port `6364`:",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE8016",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8017",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE8017",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```bash\nsudo ufw allow from 172.17.0.0/16 to any port 6364 proto tcp\n```",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE8017",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8018",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE8018",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8019",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE801A"
    ],
    "title": "### 3. Add Remote & Fetch Tracking Heads",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE8019",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE8019",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Point the remote URL to the host's Docker bridge gateway (`172.17.0.1`):",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE8019",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE801A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE801A",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```bash\n# Verify bridge gateway IP\ndocker network inspect bridge --format '{{(index .IPAM.Config 0).Gateway}}'\n\n# Register remote and fetch remote-tracking reference\ntdb remote add admin/aperas_apeiron remote_node \"http://172.17.0.1:6364/admin/aperas_apeiron\"\ntdb fetch admin/aperas_apeiron --remote=remote_node --user=admin --password=<password>\n```",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE801A",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE801B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE801B",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE801C",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE801D"
    ],
    "title": "### 4. Inspect Remote Tracking State Read-Only",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE801C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE801C",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Inspect fetched remote branches before merging into local state:",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE801C",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE801D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE801D",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```bash\n# View remote commit log\ntdb log admin/aperas_apeiron/remote_node/branch/main | less\n\n# View remote document content\nTERMINUSDB_DB_SPEC=\"admin/aperas_apeiron/remote_node/branch/main\" Aperas/scripts/tdb-doc.sh --id=\"ArtifactNode/Aperas-dev-status.md\"\n```",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE801D",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE801E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE801E",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE801F"
    ],
    "title": "## 6. Backup & Recovery Operations",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE801F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE801F",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE801G",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE801J"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAQE801F",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE801G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE801G",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE801H"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAQE801G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE801H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE801H",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Whole-Volume Tarball (`Aperas/scripts/restore.sh backup-full | verify-full | restore-full`)**:\n  **Primary adopted backup & transfer mechanism**. Captures consistent cold snapshots of `terminusdb_storage` for cross-machine host transfers.",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE801H",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE801J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE801J",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE801K"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPAQE801J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAQE801K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAQE801K",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Same-Store Snapshot (`Aperas/scripts/restore.sh backup | verify | restore`)**:\n  CLI `.bundle` exports are restricted to same-instance local rollbacks only (due to cross-store layer reference incompatibility issue #2509).",
    "title": "00C5FPAQE801K",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX0000",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0001"
    ],
    "title": "Document Root",
    "type": "root",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX0001",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0002",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0003",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0005"
    ],
    "title": "# Upstream issue: `bundle`/`unbundle` cannot move data between two independent stores",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX0002",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Filed against `terminusdb/terminusdb` as [#2509](https://github.com/terminusdb/terminusdb/issues/2509) (2026-08-26). Related: [#1147](https://github.com/terminusdb/terminusdb/issues/1147), [#1235](https://github.com/terminusdb/terminusdb/pull/1235).",
    "title": "00C5FPARX0002",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX0003",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0004"
    ],
    "title": "## Title",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX0004",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`bundle`/`unbundle` cannot move data between two independent stores — even on the same host (reproducible; related to #1147, #1235)",
    "title": "00C5FPARX0004",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX0005",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0006",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0009",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000Q",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000T",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0016",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0018"
    ],
    "title": "## Body",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX0006",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0007",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0008"
    ],
    "title": "### Summary",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX0007",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`terminusdb bundle`/`terminusdb unbundle` (CLI) only round-trips correctly when the destination is the **same store** that produced the bundle (i.e. a different database within the same running server/storage directory). The moment the destination is a genuinely **different store** — a separate `store init`, even one created moments earlier from the identical Docker image, on the identical physical machine — `unbundle` deterministically fails with `unknown_layer_reference`.",
    "title": "00C5FPARX0007",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX0008",
    "children": [],
    "text": "This is very likely the same underlying bug reported in #1147 (closed as not planned, unreproduced by maintainers) and investigated without success in #1235. I believe I've found the reason #1235's tests didn't catch it: every test in `tests/test/cli-bundle.js` calls `cli.store.init()` exactly once in the top-level `before()` hook and shares that single store across all three tests — so none of them ever exercise a bundle moving between two *different* stores, which is the one scenario that actually fails.",
    "title": "00C5FPARX0008",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX0009",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000A"
    ],
    "title": "### Environment",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX000A",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000B",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000D",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000F",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000H",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000K",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000N"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPARX000A",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX000B",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000C"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPARX000B",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX000C",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`terminusdb/terminusdb-server:v12` (Docker image), pinned digest `sha256:385faf298ad77aaf2d4d6df5e84a4cbe3596d01dab2e3b991af905639ae56388`",
    "title": "00C5FPARX000C",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX000D",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000E"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPARX000D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX000E",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`TerminusDB v12.0.7 (57f2093baeafd65e16004e84b7b58e0c5cf72858)`",
    "title": "00C5FPARX000E",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX000F",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000G"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPARX000F",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX000G",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`terminusdb-store v0.19.8`",
    "title": "00C5FPARX000G",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX000H",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000J"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPARX000H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX000J",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Confirmed identical versions on two independent physical machines (originally reported as a cross-machine issue), **and** reproduced with two containers on a single machine (see below) — ruling out network/host/version/edition as factors.",
    "title": "00C5FPARX000J",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX000K",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000M"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPARX000K",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX000M",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Community edition (no license key). The only documented guarantee for moving a database between servers I could find (https://terminusdb.org/docs/enterprise-backup-restore/) is explicitly scoped to Enterprise edition and uses a different mechanism (`/api/bundle` + `/api/unbundle` REST endpoints, target database pre-created). This report is about the CLI `bundle`/`unbundle` commands in Community edition.",
    "title": "00C5FPARX000M",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX000N",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000P"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPARX000N",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX000P",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`auto-optimize` community plugin (probabilistic layer squash/GC) was disabled for all tests below (moved `/plugins/auto-optimize.pl` out and restarted) to rule it out as a factor. Made no difference.",
    "title": "00C5FPARX000P",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX000Q",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000R",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000S"
    ],
    "title": "### Reproduction (single machine, two independent stores)",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX000R",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```bash\n# Store A: existing long-running instance\ndocker run -d --name tdb-a -p 6363:6363 -v tdb_storage_a:/app/terminusdb/storage terminusdb/terminusdb-server:v12\n\n# Store B: brand-new, independent instance, same image, same host\ndocker run -d --name tdb-b -p 6364:6363 -v tdb_storage_b:/app/terminusdb/storage terminusdb/terminusdb-server:v12\n\n# In store B: create a minimal scratch database\ndocker exec tdb-b terminusdb db create admin/test --schema=true\ndocker exec tdb-b terminusdb doc insert admin/test --graph-type=schema \\\n  --data='{\"@type\":\"Class\",\"@id\":\"Person\",\"@key\":{\"@type\":\"Random\"},\"name\":\"xsd:string\"}' -m \"schema\"\ndocker exec tdb-b terminusdb doc insert admin/test --data='{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"Test1\"}' -m \"commit 1\"\ndocker exec tdb-b terminusdb bundle admin/test -o /tmp/test.bundle\ndocker cp tdb-b:/tmp/test.bundle ./test.bundle\n\n# Positive control: unbundle back into store B itself (a different db name, same store) — works\ndocker cp ./test.bundle tdb-b:/tmp/test.bundle\ndocker exec tdb-b terminusdb db create admin/test_verify\ndocker exec tdb-b terminusdb unbundle admin/test_verify /tmp/test.bundle\n# => \"Unbundle successful\"\n\n# The actual test: unbundle into store A (different store, same host, same image/version)\ndocker cp ./test.bundle tdb-a:/tmp/test.bundle\ndocker exec tdb-a terminusdb db create admin/test_verify\ndocker exec tdb-a terminusdb unbundle admin/test_verify /tmp/test.bundle\n# => Error: error(unknown_layer_reference(\"<hash>\"))\n```",
    "title": "00C5FPARX000R",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX000S",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Result is 100% deterministic across repeated runs and across multiple independent bundle files (I tested this against three separate scratch databases with different content/commit counts, always the same failure mode, always a different specific missing-layer hash each time).",
    "title": "00C5FPARX000S",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX000T",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000V"
    ],
    "title": "### What this rules out",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX000V",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000W",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000Y",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0010",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0012",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0014"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPARX000V",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX000W",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000X"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPARX000W",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX000X",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Version mismatch** — both stores run the exact same image digest.",
    "title": "00C5FPARX000X",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX000Y",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000Z"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPARX000Y",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX000Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX000Z",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**`auto-optimize` plugin** — disabled on both stores before testing; no change.",
    "title": "00C5FPARX000Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX0010",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0011"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPARX0010",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0011",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX0011",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Store \"age\"** — reproduced with a store that was `store init`'d seconds before the test, same as the destination.",
    "title": "00C5FPARX0011",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX0012",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0013"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPARX0012",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0013",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX0013",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Network/transport corruption** — reproduced with both stores on one machine, files moved via `docker cp` only.",
    "title": "00C5FPARX0013",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0014",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX0014",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0015"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPARX0014",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0015",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX0015",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Content-specific corruption** — reproduced with a minimal, freshly-created 6-commit scratch database, not just a large/organically-evolved one.",
    "title": "00C5FPARX0015",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0016",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX0016",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0017"
    ],
    "title": "### What still works",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0017",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX0017",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Bundling and unbundling **within the same store** (different database, same running server/storage directory) works reliably every time, including after forced/probabilistic layer squashes.",
    "title": "00C5FPARX0017",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0018",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX0018",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0019",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX001E"
    ],
    "title": "### Ask",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX0019",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX0019",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX001A",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX001C"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPARX0019",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX001A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX001A",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX001B"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPARX001A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX001B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX001B",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Given #1235's tests never actually exercise the two-store case, would a PR adding that missing test case (spin up two `store.init()` stores, bundle from one, unbundle into the other) be welcome, to at least turn this into a real reproducible regression test?",
    "title": "00C5FPARX001B",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX001C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX001C",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPARX001D"
    ],
    "title": "00C5FPARX001C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX001D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX001D",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Is cross-store portability of `bundle`/`unbundle` intended to work at all in Community edition, or is it only ever meant for same-store snapshot/restore (with genuine cross-server moves being an Enterprise-only capability, as the backup-restore docs suggest)? If the latter, it'd be worth stating explicitly in the CLI docs/help text, since \"a pack ... that can then be reconstituted\" (the current `bundle --help` description) reads as store-agnostic.",
    "title": "00C5FPARX001D",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPARX001E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPARX001E",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Related: #1147, #1235",
    "title": "00C5FPARX001E",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATB8000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATB8000",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPATB8001"
    ],
    "title": "Document Root",
    "type": "root",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATB8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATB8001",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPATB8002",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPATB8003",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG001"
    ],
    "title": "# Upstream issue: property-level `@unfold: true` is a no-op on `List` properties",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATB8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATB8002",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Filed against `terminusdb/terminusdb` as [#2512](https://github.com/terminusdb/terminusdb/issues/2512) (2026-08-29). Related: [#2321](https://github.com/terminusdb/terminusdb/pull/2321) (introduced field-level `@unfold`).",
    "title": "00C64YY0C0002",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATB8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATB8003",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG000"
    ],
    "title": "## Title",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG000",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Field-level `@unfold: true` is a no-op on `List`-typed properties (works on `Set`/`Optional`/`Cardinality`); likely a gap in #2321",
    "title": "00C64YY0C0004",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG001",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG002",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG003",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG004",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG009",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG00A",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG00B",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG00C",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG00D",
      "BlockNode/00C64YY0C000J",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG00F",
      "BlockNode/00C64YY0C000Z",
      "BlockNode/00C64YY0C0010",
      "BlockNode/00C64YY0C0011",
      "BlockNode/00C64YY0C0012",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG00Y",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG017",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG018",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG019",
      "BlockNode/00C64YY0C001D",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG01G"
    ],
    "title": "## Body",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG002",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Describe the bug**\nProperty-level `\"@unfold\": true` (added in #2321) works correctly for `Optional`, `Set`, and `Cardinality` properties, but is silently ignored for `List` properties: the field is returned as plain id references, with no error or warning. Class-level `@unfoldable` on the target class does not have this problem, it correctly unfolds through `List` properties, including recursive self-referential ones.",
    "title": "00C64YY0C0006",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG003",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Docs describe `List` as supported, with the same example syntax as the other container types:",
    "title": "00C64YY0C0007",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG004",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG005",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG007"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C64YY0C0008",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG005",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG006"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YY0C0009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG006",
    "children": [],
    "text": "https://terminusdb.org/docs/document-unfolding-reference/: table listing \"List: `{ \"@type\": \"List\", \"@class\": \"Customer\", \"@unfold\": true }`\" under \"works with all property type families\"",
    "title": "00C64YY0C000A",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG007",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG008"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YY0C000B",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG008",
    "children": [],
    "text": "https://terminusdb.org/docs/schema-reference-guide/: \"Add `\"@unfold\": true` to any complex property definition (Optional, Set, Array, List, or Cardinality)\"",
    "title": "00C64YY0C000C",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG009",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**To Reproduce**\nSteps to reproduce the behavior:",
    "title": "00C64YY0C000D",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG00A",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```\ndocker exec tdb terminusdb db create admin/unfold_test --schema=true\ndocker exec tdb terminusdb doc insert admin/unfold_test --graph-type=schema --data='[\n  {\"@type\":\"Class\",\"@id\":\"Item\",\"@key\":{\"@type\":\"Lexical\",\"@fields\":[\"name\"]},\"name\":\"xsd:string\"},\n  {\"@type\":\"Class\",\"@id\":\"SetHolder\",\"@key\":{\"@type\":\"Lexical\",\"@fields\":[\"name\"]},\n   \"name\":\"xsd:string\",\"items\":{\"@type\":\"Set\",\"@class\":\"Item\",\"@unfold\":true}},\n  {\"@type\":\"Class\",\"@id\":\"ListHolder\",\"@key\":{\"@type\":\"Lexical\",\"@fields\":[\"name\"]},\n   \"name\":\"xsd:string\",\"items\":{\"@type\":\"List\",\"@class\":\"Item\",\"@unfold\":true}}\n]' -m \"schema\"\n\ndocker exec tdb terminusdb doc insert admin/unfold_test --data='[\n  {\"@type\":\"Item\",\"name\":\"i1\"},\n  {\"@type\":\"Item\",\"name\":\"i2\"},\n  {\"@type\":\"SetHolder\",\"name\":\"sh1\",\"items\":[\"Item/i1\",\"Item/i2\"]},\n  {\"@type\":\"ListHolder\",\"name\":\"lh1\",\"items\":[\"Item/i1\",\"Item/i2\"]}\n]' -m \"data\"\n\ndocker exec tdb terminusdb doc get admin/unfold_test --id=SetHolder/sh1\n# => items unfolds inline: \"items\":[{\"@id\":\"Item/i1\",\"@type\":\"Item\",\"name\":\"i1\"}, ...]\n\ndocker exec tdb terminusdb doc get admin/unfold_test --id=ListHolder/lh1\n# => items stays as bare refs: \"items\":[\"Item/i1\",\"Item/i2\"]   <-- @unfold:true had no effect\n```",
    "title": "00C64YY0C000E",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG00B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG00B",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Current behavior**\n`ListHolder.items` (a `List` with `@unfold: true`) is returned as bare id references. Confirmed this is independent of the request-level `unfold` query/CLI flag: passing `unfold=true` or `unfold=false` explicitly made no observable difference in either direction for either class, only the schema-level annotations (`@unfold`, `@unfoldable`) determine the outcome.",
    "title": "00C64YY0C000F",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG00C",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Expected behavior**\n`ListHolder.items` unfolds inline, the same as `SetHolder.items` does, matching the docs linked above.",
    "title": "00C64YY0C000G",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG00D",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**What still works**\nMarking the target class `@unfoldable: []` (class-level) instead of the property `@unfold: true` correctly unfolds `List` properties, including through a self-referential recursive `List<Self>` (verified 3 levels deep, cycle-protected). So the container-type gap is specific to the property-level `@unfold` mechanism, not to unfolding-through-`List` in general.",
    "title": "00C64YY0C000H",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG00E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG00E",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Info (please complete the following information):**",
    "title": "00C5FPATBG00E",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:26.224Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
