    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG00T"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YY0C000X",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG00T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG00T",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`terminusdb-store v0.19.8`",
    "title": "00C64YY0C000Y",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG00V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG00V",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Additional context**\nTraced the likely root cause into the #2321 diff. `json.pl`'s unfold decision predicate (added by #2321):",
    "title": "00C5FPATBG00V",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:26.224Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG00W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG00W",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```prolog\nshould_unfold_property(DB, _ParentId, _P, TargetClass) :-\n    is_subdocument(DB, TargetClass), !.\nshould_unfold_property(DB, _ParentId, _P, TargetClass) :-\n    is_unfoldable(DB, TargetClass), !.\nshould_unfold_property(DB, ParentId, P, _TargetClass) :-\n    instance_of(DB, ParentId, ParentClass),\n    property_is_unfold(DB, ParentClass, P, true), !.\n```",
    "title": "00C5FPATBG00W",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:26.224Z",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG00X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG00X",
    "children": [],
    "text": "The third clause (property-level `@unfold`) needs `ParentId` plus the property name `P` to look up `property_is_unfold/4`. The first two clauses need only `TargetClass`, resolvable from anywhere.",
    "title": "00C5FPATBG00X",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:26.224Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG00Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG00Y",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG00Z",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG011",
      "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG013"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C64YY0C0013",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG00Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG00Z",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YY0C0015"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YY0C0014",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG010",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`List`-typed values are represented internally as an RDF Collection: a chain of `Cons` cells linked by `rdf:first`/`rdf:rest`, not a direct edge from the parent to the target instance.",
    "title": "00C5FPATBG010",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:26.224Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG011",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG011",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YY0C0017"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YY0C0016",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG012",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Confirmed via raw triple inspection: a `Set` property's target is one hop from the parent; a `List` property's target is behind two additional hops, through an intermediate `Cons` node.",
    "title": "00C5FPATBG012",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:26.224Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG013",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG013",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YY0C0019"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YY0C0018",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG014",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG014",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Per the #2321 diff, `List` materialization goes through a separate, pre-existing routine, `list_type_id_predicate_value/8`, which does not call `should_unfold_property/3` at all. So the property-level `@unfold` signal (clause 3 above, tied to `ParentId`/`P`) never reaches the code that walks the `Cons` chain.",
    "title": "00C5FPATBG014",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:26.224Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG015",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG015",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FPATBG015",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:26.224Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG016",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG016",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Class-level `@unfoldable` (clause 2 above) keeps working regardless, because it only needs the target class, which is still resolvable at each `Cons` hop through whatever does check it there.",
    "title": "00C5FPATBG016",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:26.224Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG017",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG017",
    "children": [],
    "text": "The PR's own test for `List` only asserts the schema round-trips the annotation, never that it actually unfolds at read time:",
    "title": "00C64YY0C001A",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG018",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG018",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```javascript\nit('should accept @unfold on List property', async function () {\n  ...\n  const r2 = await document.get(agent, { query: { graph_type: 'schema', id: 'Sequence' } })\n  expect(r2.body.elements['@unfold']).to.equal(true)\n})\n```",
    "title": "00C64YY0C001B",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG019",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG019",
    "children": [],
    "text": "That's why it passes CI regardless of whether unfolding actually happens at read time.",
    "title": "00C64YY0C001C",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG01A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG01A",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Two open questions for maintainers:",
    "title": "00C5FPATBG01A",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:26.224Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG01B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG01B",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FPATBG01B",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:26.224Z",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG01C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG01C",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FPATBG01C",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:26.224Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG01D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG01D",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Is `List` support for property-level `@unfold` intended (matching the docs), making this a bug in the `list_type_id_predicate_value/8` path? Or was `List` never actually meant to be supported at the property level, only via class-level `@unfoldable`, making this a docs bug in `document-unfolding-reference` and `schema-reference-guide` instead?",
    "title": "00C5FPATBG01D",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:26.224Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG01E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG01E",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FPATBG01E",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:26.224Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG01F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG01F",
    "children": [],
    "text": "If the former, would a PR adding an actual data-retrieval test for the `List` case (not just the schema round-trip currently in `field-level-unfold.js`) be welcome, to close the CI gap that let this ship?",
    "title": "00C5FPATBG01F",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:26.224Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPATBG01G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPATBG01G",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Related: #2321",
    "title": "00C64YY0C001E",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FQW6CR019",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FQW6CR019",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`FolderNode` — **implemented and live-verified** (`Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §4.A). `web/src/lib/folders.ts` walks `AperasKG/artifacts/`, builds one `FolderNode` per directory, absorbs each directory's own `README.md` (parsed blocks become the folder's children; the file itself is never exposed as a separate `ArtifactNode`), and references nested `FolderNode`s/`ArtifactNode`s by id. Wired into `npm run kg:ingest`, which now rebuilds the whole folder tree in the same run as artifact ingestion. Added one concrete `Assertion` class (inherits the previously-uninstantiable abstract `BaseEdge`) to `schema.json`, needed to let `crud.ts`/`woql.ts` actually write/query extrinsic edges — documented in `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §2.D. `FolderNode`/`ArtifactNode` are now Snowflake-keyed (`folderId`/`artifactId`), `path` a plain mutable field — see the \"Reconciliation matching\" entry below for the full migration.",
    "title": "00C5FQW6CR019",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FQW6CR01E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FQW6CR01E",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FQW6CR01E",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FQW6CR01F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FQW6CR01F",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Heading levels now define tree structure** — **implemented and live-verified**. `astParser.ts` gained `groupByHeadings`, a one-pass depth-stack transform run on every flat mdast sibling list before conversion: each heading becomes the parent of everything until a heading of depth <= its own. A doc with `# Title` / `## Section A` / `## Section B` now parses as nested (`Title` containing `Section A`, `Section B`, each with their own body), not a flat list under the root. Alongside this: every `BlockNode` now carries its raw mdast `type` (needed by reconciliation's leaf/container split below), and `list`/`listItem`/`blockquote` no longer carry the full-subtree-duplicate `text` they used to (confirmed live pre-fix: a `listItem`'s `text` byte-for-byte duplicated its own paragraph child's) — containers now carry no content of their own, by design.",
    "title": "00C5FQW6CR01F",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FQW6CR01G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FQW6CR01G",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FQW6CR01G",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FQW6CR01H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FQW6CR01H",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Reconciliation matching for re-ingestion** — **implemented and live-verified** (`Aperas-reconciliation-matching-design.md`, `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §1.B/§4.A/§4.B/Appendix G). New `web/src/lib/reconcile.ts`: a Gestalt (Ratcliff/Obershelp) tree diff — the longest-common-run algorithm behind Python's `difflib` — applied two-stage per level (Stage A anchors on leaf content by `heading XOR text`; Stage B aligns containers by type within the segments Stage A's anchors define), with ambiguous same-content duplicates declined rather than guessed. Matched `BlockNode`s reuse their old `blockId`; unmatched old ones get an explicit `tombstonedAt` (new field on `BaseNode`, inherited everywhere) rather than being silently orphaned; a block relocated to a different section is detected as a cross-parent move via the same mechanism, one level up from per-parent matching. `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode` moved off `Lexical`-on-`path` to Snowflake ids (`artifactId`/`folderId`, same scheme as `BlockNode.blockId`), `path` now a plain mutable field with `title`/`text` added to `ArtifactNode` (filename / naive first-paragraph abstract, matching `FolderNode`'s existing shape) — this is what makes a file/folder rename a field update instead of a delete-and-recreate. Rename detection reuses the identical Gestalt-matching primitive one level up: on every `kg:track`/`kg:ingest` sweep, disk-only and DB-only leftover paths are matched by abstract-text similarity (`matchLeftoverByAbstract`) before falling back to plain add/remove. Wired into `ingestArtifact` (fires whenever a prior ingestion exists), `trackAllArtifacts`, and `ingestFolderTree`; `kgCli.ts` reports renamed/removed/reconciled counts alongside the existing tracked/ingested counts. Live-verified via `verifyPhase0.ts` (edit-and-reingest keeps unrelated `blockId`s stable, reports sane unchanged/added counts) and a manual rename test against a throwaway artifact (`artifactId` and `blockId`s survived a real on-disk move). Migrating the key scheme required clearing all pre-existing `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode`/`BlockNode` documents first, since TerminusDB rejects a schema whose new required fields the old instance data doesn't have — the whole KG was then rebuilt from `AperasKG/artifacts/` via a full `kg:track` + `kg:ingest` sweep, per the project's disk-is-source-of-truth model.",
    "title": "00C5FQW6CR01H",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FQW6D0008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FQW6D0008",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Phase 2+ skills: ingestion-from-arbitrary-sources, graph search skill, refactoring/lazy-atomization skill.",
    "title": "00C5FQW6D0008",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FQW6D000A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FQW6D000A",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Reconciling separate hosts' diverged `aperas_apeiron` histories (push/pull, possibly rebase) — currently only fetched-and-inspected, not merged.",
    "title": "00C5FQW6D000A",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET000B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET000B",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```\nAperas/                               # Core Engine (Maintained by Core Dev Team)\n├── scripts/                          # Universal infrastructure & DB operational tooling\n│   ├── restore.sh                    # Backup, restore & verification suite\n│   ├── tdb-log.sh                    # Local-time commit log helper (default count: 20)\n│   └── tdb-doc.sh                    # Local-time document inspection helper\n├── skills/                           # Core agent skill definitions\n│   └── terminusdb/                   # TerminusDB operational reference skill\n├── web/                              # TypeScript project for substrate transducers & UI\n│   └── src/lib/                      # Core data access, AST transducer & schema modules\n│\n└── AperasKG/                         # Domain KG (Maintained by Community)\n    ├── artifacts/                    # Plain-text Markdown domain projections & documentation\n    ├── Apeiron/                      # Portable JSON-LD substrate mirror (schema + instances), bidirectional — see §5\n    ├── schema/                       # Domain-specific JSON-LD schemas extending core\n    ├── ontology/                     # Domain-specific predicate taxonomy / vocabularies\n    └── transducers/                  # Domain-specific ingestion/parsing scripts\n```",
    "title": "00C64YWET000B",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET8006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET8006",
    "children": [],
    "text": "| Module | Location | Responsibilities & Protocol Constraints |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Client Manager** | `web/src/lib/client.ts` | Configures `TerminusDB.WOQLClient`, creates `aperas_apeiron` database, applies idempotent schema initialization via `full_replace` from `schema.json`. |\n| **Node Identity** | `web/src/lib/snowflake.ts` | Generates the 64-bit Snowflake-style `blockId` (timestamp + machine identity + sequence, 13-char Crockford Base32) — see `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §1.A. |\n| **AST Transducer** | `web/src/lib/astParser.ts` | Uses `unified.js` (`remark-parse`) to recursively convert Markdown into a nested `BlockNode` tree, assigning each block a fresh Snowflake id via `snowflake.ts` (identity is never derived from content or position). |\n| **Artifact Tracking & Ingestion** | `web/src/lib/artifacts.ts` | Computes `fileHash`, tracks/upserts lightweight `ArtifactNode`s, and ingests the full `BlockNode` tree on change — see §4 below. |\n| **Folder Ingestion** | `web/src/lib/folders.ts` | Walks `AperasKG/artifacts/` and commits the `FolderNode` structural tree — see §4 below. |\n| **Extrinsic Assertion CRUD** | `web/src/lib/crud.ts` | `insertAssertion`/`deleteAssertionsInvolvingNode` for the concrete `Assertion` type (source/predicate/target, node-typed per §3 of the design doc's rejection of the `xsd:string` anti-pattern), plus generic best-effort document delete helpers. |\n| **WOQL Engine** | `web/src/lib/woql.ts` | Builds and executes WOQL queries over `Assertion` — `queryNodeAssertions` (both directions) and `traceImpactPropagation` (one-hop sweep along a predicate like `impacts`). |\n| **GraphQL Client** | `web/src/lib/graphql.ts` | `getArtifactTreeViaGraphQL` fetches an `ArtifactNode` and its full nested `BlockNode` tree (bounded depth) via the auto-generated GraphQL endpoint — see the note below on why this is the *only* full-tree read path. |\n| **Version Control** | `web/src/lib/versionControl.ts` | Manages branches, temporal commit histories, version diffing, merge applications (`apply`), and state resets. Class-agnostic — unaffected by the schema redesign. |\n| **JSON-LD Import/Export** | `web/src/lib/export.ts` | `exportJsonLd`/`importJsonLd` mirror the current schema plus every instance document (per class) between TerminusDB and plain JSON-LD files in `AperasKG/Apeiron/` — see §5. |",
    "title": "00C64YWET8006",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET800G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET800G",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET800H",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET800J",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET800K",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET800R",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET800T"
    ],
    "title": "## 5. JSON-LD Substrate Import/Export",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET800H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET800H",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`web/src/lib/export.ts`, wired through `kgCli.ts`, bidirectionally mirrors the schema and every instance document between TerminusDB and plain JSON-LD files in `AperasKG/Apeiron/`:",
    "title": "00C64YWET800H",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET800J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET800J",
    "children": [],
    "text": "| File | Contents |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| `schema.jsonld` | The full schema graph (`getDocument({ graph_type: 'schema' })`), verbatim. |\n| `ArtifactNode.jsonld`, `FolderNode.jsonld`, `BlockNode.jsonld`, `Assertion.jsonld` | One file per instance class — a leading `@context` document, then every live (`getDocument({ type, as_list: true })`) instance of that class, sorted by id for diff-stable re-exports. |",
    "title": "00C64YWET800J",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET800K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET800K",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET800M",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET800P"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C64YWET800K",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET800M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET800M",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET800N"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWET800M",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET800N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET800N",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**`npm run kg:export`** — writes all of the above from the current TerminusDB state, overwriting the files.",
    "title": "00C64YWET800N",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET800P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET800P",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET800Q"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWET800P",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET800Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET800Q",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**`npm run kg:import`** — reads the files back: applies `schema.jsonld` via `full_replace`, then upserts each class's instances (every document already carries its own `@id`, so a matching document is updated in place, not duplicated). Each class is submitted as a single batched `updateDocument` call, in the dependency order `BlockNode` → `ArtifactNode` → `FolderNode` → `Assertion`, so a document is never written before something it references — `BlockNode`'s own parent/child references resolve within its own batch (one commit, so intra-batch forward references are fine); everything after it can then safely reference already-committed ids. Every write is its own TerminusDB commit, so before writing the schema or a given class, its content hash is compared (`hashDocSet` in `client.ts` — the same order-independent hash already used to skip a no-op schema apply) against what's currently live, and the write is skipped entirely when nothing changed, rather than landing a no-op commit.",
    "title": "00C64YWET800Q",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET800R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET800R",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET800S"
    ],
    "title": "### Purpose: how `AperasKG` holds a backup of its own KG",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET800S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET800S",
    "children": [],
    "text": "This round-trip — not a TerminusDB-level backup — is the correct answer to \"how does `AperasKG` hold a record of its KG,\" per its original design goal of storing both the artifacts and the KG. `AperasKG/Apeiron/` is the canonical graph content, materialized as plain, diffable JSON-LD text and committed to the same git repository as `AperasKG/artifacts/` — an ordinary `git commit` over that directory *is* the KG's backup, with all the history, diffing, and portability that implies, and `kg:import` is the restore path (bootstrap a fresh database, or recover state) back out of it. This also happens to make the content engine-agnostic — `AperasKG/Apeiron/` is a snapshot any future substrate engine could read without a bespoke migration script (see `Aperas-design.md`'s Development Roadmap, \"Phase 4: Substrate Evolution\") — but that's a secondary benefit of the same design, not the primary reason it exists.",
    "title": "00C64YWET800S",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET800T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET800T",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET800V"
    ],
    "title": "### Scope and non-goals",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET800V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET800V",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET800W",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET800Y",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET8010"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C64YWET800V",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET800W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET800W",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET800X"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWET800W",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET800X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET800X",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Flat, not nested.** Instances are dumped and read back exactly as `getDocument`/`updateDocument` handle them — `BlockNode.children` and `ArtifactNode.root` are reference ids, not inlined subtrees (see §2's \"Read-path note\"), matching how TerminusDB itself stores documents and keeping per-class diffs scoped to that class alone.",
    "title": "00C64YWET800X",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET800Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET800Y",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET800Z"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWET800Y",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET800Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET800Z",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Includes tombstoned documents.** The export/import round-trip is a full audit snapshot, not a live-only view — reconciliation's `tombstonedAt` markers (`Aperas-reconciliation-matching-design.md`) are preserved rather than filtered out.",
    "title": "00C64YWET800Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET8010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET8010",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET8011"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWET8010",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET8011",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET8011",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Whole-class granularity, not a merge.** Import upserts every document in a class file; it doesn't diff against the live database or reconcile divergence — reconciliation (`reconcile.ts`) only ever runs against `AperasKG/artifacts/` content during `kg:ingest`, not against this export/import path.",
    "title": "00C64YWET8011",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET8012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET8012",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET8013",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET8014",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET801C"
    ],
    "title": "## 6. TerminusDB Server Operational Backup",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET8013",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET8013",
    "children": [],
    "text": "This section is server infrastructure for the TerminusDB instance itself — Docker-volume-level disaster recovery, unrelated to `AperasKG`'s own record of its content. It answers \"how do I recover this TerminusDB server if its volume is lost,\" not \"how does `AperasKG` hold a backup of its KG.\" That second question is answered by §5: `AperasKG/Apeiron/` plus `kg:export`/`kg:import`, git-tracked alongside `AperasKG/artifacts/` like any other content in the domain-KG repo — not by storing TerminusDB-level snapshots in or near `AperasKG` at all, which an earlier design iteration tried (`db/` briefly lived under `AperasKG/`) before being reconsidered as the wrong coupling: a git-tracked domain repo has no good way to diff, merge, or meaningfully version an opaque binary DB snapshot, and (per the investigation below) those snapshots aren't even portable between independent TerminusDB stores.",
    "title": "00C64YWET8013",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET8014",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET8014",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET8015"
    ],
    "title": "### Whole-Volume Disaster Recovery (`restore.sh backup-full | verify-full | restore-full`)",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET8015",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET8015",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET8016",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET8018",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET801A"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C64YWET8015",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET8016",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET8016",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET8017"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWET8016",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET8017",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET8017",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Primary Adopted Method**: Creates a tarball of the backing Docker volume `terminusdb_storage` via a temporary Alpine container with the TerminusDB container temporarily stopped to ensure on-disk head consistency.",
    "title": "00C64YWET8017",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET8018",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET8018",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET8019"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWET8018",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET8019",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET8019",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Scope**: **Cross-Machine Host Transfer**.",
    "title": "00C64YWET8019",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET801A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET801A",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET801B"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWET801A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET801B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET801B",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Restore Safety**: `restore-full` extracts into an isolated temporary volume/container (`<container>-restored`) for inspection. Automatic promotion (`--overwrite`) updates container volume bindings with automatic fallback to `-old` on startup failure.",
    "title": "00C64YWET801B",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET801C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET801C",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET801D"
    ],
    "title": "### Same-Store Snapshot (`restore.sh backup | verify | restore`)",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET801D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET801D",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET801E",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET801G"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C64YWET801D",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET801E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET801E",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET801F"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWET801E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET801F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET801F",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Mechanism**: Wraps TerminusDB `bundle` / `unbundle` CLI commands. `backup` self-verifies by unbundling into a temporary verification database.",
    "title": "00C64YWET801F",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET801G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET801G",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET801H"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWET801G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET801H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET801H",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Scope**: **Same-instance snapshot & local rollback only**. CLI `.bundle` exports suffer from cross-store layer reference incompatibility (issue #2509) and cannot be transferred across independent TerminusDB server instances.",
    "title": "00C64YWET801H",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET801J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET801J",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET801K",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET801M"
    ],
    "title": "## 7. SSH-Tunneled Remotes",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET801K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET801K",
    "children": [],
    "text": "TerminusDB remotes communicate over HTTP REST endpoints. Cross-machine communication between separate hosts utilizes SSH local port forwarding:",
    "title": "00C64YWET801K",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET801M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET801M",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET801N",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET801Q",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET801S",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET801V",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET801X"
    ],
    "ordered": true,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C64YWET801M",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET801N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET801N",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET801P"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWET801N",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET801P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET801P",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Transport Rationale**: Native remote commands (`push`/`pull`/`fetch`/`clone`) speak HTTP(S) only. TerminusDB itself listens on `0.0.0.0:6363` inside the container (confirmed via `/proc/net/tcp`) — the loopback-only restriction (`127.0.0.1:6363`) is this project's own `docker run -p 127.0.0.1:6363:6363` deployment choice, not a TerminusDB default. Either way, this project's containers are loopback-only, so cross-machine transport requires an SSH tunnel.",
    "title": "00C64YWET801P",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET801Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET801Q",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET801R"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWET801Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET801R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET801R",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Tunnel Endpoint**: `ssh -N -f -L 0.0.0.0:6364:localhost:6363 <user>@<remote-host>`",
    "title": "00C64YWET801R",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET801S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET801S",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET801T"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWET801S",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET801T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET801T",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Firewall Access**: `sudo ufw allow from 172.17.0.0/16 to any port 6364 proto tcp`",
    "title": "00C64YWET801T",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET801V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET801V",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET801W"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWET801V",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET801W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET801W",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Bridge Addressing**: Remote URLs target the host's Docker bridge gateway (`http://172.17.0.1:6364/admin/aperas_apeiron`).",
    "title": "00C64YWET801W",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET801X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET801X",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET801Y"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWET801X",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET801Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET801Y",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Remote Tracking**: `fetch` updates local remote-tracking descriptors (`<org>/<db>/<remote>/branch/<branch>`). `fetch` must be executed before `push` or `pull` can resolve remote heads.",
    "title": "00C64YWET801Y",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET801Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET801Z",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET8020"
    ],
    "title": "## 8. Verification & Operational Utilities",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET8020",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET8020",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET8021",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET8023",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET8025"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C64YWET8020",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET8021",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET8021",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET8022"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWET8021",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET8022",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET8022",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Verification Test Harness**: `npm run verify:phase0 -- --db` (`web/src/lib/verifyPhase0.ts`) — end-to-end, idempotent, self-cleaning live test: AST parsing, schema init, artifact track/ingest, GraphQL tree read, `FolderNode` ingestion, `Assertion` CRUD + WOQL impact propagation, and temporal commit management (branch + commit log). Demo-state cleanup has to happen in reference-reversed order — `FolderNode` before `ArtifactNode` before its `BlockNode`s — since TerminusDB enforces referential integrity and rejects deleting a still-referenced document.",
    "title": "00C64YWET8022",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET8023",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET8023",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET8024"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWET8023",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET8024",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET8024",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**`Aperas/scripts/tdb-log.sh`**: Provides compact, local-time commit history (`--count 20` by default) with fast client-side message filtering (`--filter`). Avoids sluggish `tdb history` diffs.",
    "title": "00C64YWET8024",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET8025",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET8025",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWET8026"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWET8025",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWET8026",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWET8026",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**`Aperas/scripts/tdb-doc.sh`**: Wraps `tdb doc get` to convert ISO UTC timestamps to local time and unescape literal newlines (`\\n`) into readable multi-line prose.",
    "title": "00C64YWET8026",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG000",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG001"
    ],
    "title": "Document Root",
    "type": "root",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG001",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG002",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG003",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG005",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG007",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG009",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00K",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG014",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG016"
    ],
    "title": "# Artifact Projection — Design",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG002",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §5.A names three projection modes that turn a stored\n`BlockNode` tree back into an output: Artifact Projection (serialize back to the physical\n`.md` file, always fully unfolded regardless of each block's `unfolded` state), the Human UI,\nand the Agentic BFS interface. This doc settles the design for the first of the three —\nArtifact Projection, the direct inverse of `astParser.ts`'s Markdown → tree transform. The\nother two modes are out of scope here. The design below is settled; nothing has been\nimplemented yet.",
    "title": "00C64YWTRG002",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG003",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG004"
    ],
    "title": "## 1. Canonical regeneration, not byte-exact",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG004",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`heading`/`paragraph`/`code` blocks already round-trip exactly — their `title`/`text` are raw\nsource slices, not derived summaries. Container types (`list`, `listItem`, `blockquote`) are\nregenerated as clean, valid Markdown rather than reproducing the original file's exact\nwhitespace and spacing. This matches the bar reconciliation already uses elsewhere in this\nproject: \"parses back to the same tree,\" not \"identical bytes.\"",
    "title": "00C64YWTRG004",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG005",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG006"
    ],
    "title": "## 2. List items are always blank-line-separated in the output",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG006",
    "children": [],
    "text": "mdast's `spread` (tight vs. loose list) isn't captured. CommonMark requires blank lines\nbetween list items whenever any item is \"loose\" (multi-paragraph); always emitting them is\nvalid either way and has no effect on the re-parsed tree, since remark already wraps every\nlist item's content in a paragraph regardless of the original list's tightness (a pre-existing,\nseparately-confirmed quirk — not something this design introduces). Capturing `spread` would\nonly ever affect cosmetic rendering spacing, never structure, so it's left out.",
    "title": "00C64YWTRG006",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG007",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG008"
    ],
    "title": "## 3. Blockquote line-prefixing is a projection-side concern",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG008",
    "children": [],
    "text": "CommonMark only requires the `> ` marker on a blockquote's first line (or after a blank line\nends and restarts the quote) — a continuation line needs no marker at all (\"lazy\ncontinuation\"). Whether `astParser.ts`'s raw-text slice for a multi-line paragraph inside a\n`blockquote` contains a stray `> ` on its continuation lines therefore depends on how the\nsource was actually written, not on anything the parser does: confirmed live, `\"> line\none\\n> line two\"` (marker repeated, common in practice) slices to `\"line one\\n> line two\"`\n(marker present in the leaf's own `text`), while `\"> line one\\nline two\"` (lazy continuation,\nalso valid) slices to `\"line one\\nline two\"` (nothing stray — matches mdast's own semantic\n`text.value` either way). Rather than depending on which form a given source used — or fixing\nthis at ingestion, which would perturb reconciliation's matching keys for existing blockquote\ncontent — the serializer normalizes at output time: strip any leading `> ` from each line of a\nblockquote's rendered content (a no-op when there isn't one), then re-apply `> ` uniformly.",
    "title": "00C64YWTRG008",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG009",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00A",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00B",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00C"
    ],
    "title": "## 4. New fields: `ordered`, `start`, `checked` — captured, not derived",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG00A",
    "children": [],
    "text": "A `list` node's numbered-vs-bulleted style and starting number, and a `listItem`'s task-list\ncheckbox state, aren't recoverable from anything currently stored — they have to be captured\nat parse time. mdast already carries all three directly on the relevant nodes (`list.ordered`,\n`list.start`, `listItem.checked`, confirmed live) — nothing lazy or derived about them, they\nsit on the same mdast node object `astParser.ts` already visits. They're absent from\n`ParsedBlockNode` today because `convertAstNode` was never asked to read them, not because\nthey were unavailable: it extracts `blockId`/`title`/`text`/`type`/`children` identically for\nevery node type and has never read a type-specific mdast property, since nothing downstream\nneeded one before projection made round-tripping a goal. So this is a scope gap in the\nexisting extraction logic, closed by capture — not inference of something the parser\npreviously discarded.",
    "title": "00C64YWTRG00A",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG00B",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Schema (`BlockNode`, all `Optional` — unlike the `artifactId`/`type` migration, this needs no\nDB wipe, since existing documents remain valid against new optional fields):",
    "title": "00C64YWTRG00B",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG00C",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00D",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00F",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00H"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C64YWTRG00C",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG00D",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00E"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWTRG00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG00E",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`ordered: Optional xsd:boolean` — set on `list` nodes.",
    "title": "00C64YWTRG00E",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG00F",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00G"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWTRG00F",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG00G",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`start: Optional xsd:integer` — set on `list` nodes (mdast always provides one, even for\n  unordered lists, where it's simply unused).",
    "title": "00C64YWTRG00G",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG00H",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00J"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWTRG00H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG00J",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`checked: Optional xsd:boolean` — set on `listItem` nodes only when mdast's own `checked` is\n  non-null; its absence (not `false`) is what distinguishes \"not a task item\" from \"unchecked.\"",
    "title": "00C64YWTRG00J",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG00K",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00M",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00N"
    ],
    "title": "## 5. The algorithm",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG00M",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Pure, recursive dispatch on `node.type`:",
    "title": "00C64YWTRG00M",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG00N",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00P",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00R",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00T",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00W",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00Y",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG010",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG012"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C64YWTRG00N",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG00P",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00Q"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWTRG00P",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG00Q",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**root** / any other container fallback: children rendered and joined with a blank line.",
    "title": "00C64YWTRG00Q",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG00R",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00S"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWTRG00R",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG00S",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**heading**: `title` (already the full raw heading line, `#`s included) followed by its\n  rendered children, blank-line-joined.",
    "title": "00C64YWTRG00S",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG00T",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00V"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWTRG00T",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG00V",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**paragraph**: `text`, dedented (every line but the first stripped of whatever common leading\n  whitespace they share — needed because a multi-line leaf's raw slice only has line 1's\n  container-required indentation stripped; every later line keeps its literal original-file\n  column, confirmed live on both a `blockquote` continuation line and a nested `code` fence's\n  interior — left alone, a container's own re-indentation (below) would compound on top of that\n  stale absolute value instead of establishing a clean baseline).",
    "title": "00C64YWTRG00V",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG00W",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00X"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWTRG00W",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG00X",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**code**: same dedenting, plus one more check — a *fenced* block's raw slice starts with its\n  own `` ``` ``/`~~~` marker, same as any other leaf, and is emitted as-is once dedented. An\n  *indented* (4-space) code block is also mdast type `code`, but its raw slice carries no fence\n  at all, and unlike every other leaf, line 1 isn't stripped of its marker either (confirmed\n  live — the indentation *is* the syntax marker, so it survives on every line including the\n  first). Left alone this would silently degrade into an ordinary paragraph on projection, so a\n  raw slice with no fence marker is dedented across all its lines (line 1 included) and\n  re-wrapped in a fresh generic fence — always converting indented-style input to fenced-style\n  output (§8).",
    "title": "00C64YWTRG00X",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG00Y",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00Z"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWTRG00Y",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG00Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG00Z",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**blockquote**: render children, strip a leading `> ` from every line, re-prefix every line\n  with `> ` (§3).",
    "title": "00C64YWTRG00Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG010",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG011"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWTRG010",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG011",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG011",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**list**: render each child as a list item — marker is `${n}. ` if `ordered`, else `- `,\n  with `n` starting at `start ?? 1` — joined with a blank line (§2).",
    "title": "00C64YWTRG011",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG012",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG013"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWTRG012",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG013",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG013",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**list item**: prefix = marker + (`[x] ` / `[ ] ` if `checked` is defined), body = children\n  rendered and blank-line-joined, every line after the first indented to the prefix's width.\n  This is what makes a nested `list` under a `listItem` indent correctly — it falls out of the\n  recursion for free, no special-casing needed.",
    "title": "00C64YWTRG013",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG014",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG014",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG015"
    ],
    "title": "## 6. Entry point",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG015",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG015",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`projectArtifactToMarkdown(client, path)`: fetch the tree via the existing\n`getArtifactTreeViaGraphQL` (`graphql.ts` — its field selection needs `ordered`/`start`/\n`checked` added, the same fix already needed once this session for the `type` field), then run\nthe serializer over `tree.root`. Root itself is never emitted — it falls through the generic\ncontainer fallback, which is exactly \"join my children.\"",
    "title": "00C64YWTRG015",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG016",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG016",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG017",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG018",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG019"
    ],
    "title": "## 7. Verification strategy",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG017",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG017",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Round-trip equivalence — parse a sample exercising every branch (ordered list, unordered list\nwith a task item, nested list, blockquote, code, headings) → serialize → re-parse → compare —\nis checked by reusing `reconcile.ts`'s `reconcileTree` (the original parse as `oldRoot`, the\nre-parsed result as `newRoot`): equivalence is `stats.added === 0 && stats.removed === 0`,\ni.e. every block matches. This reuses already-verified matching logic as the equivalence check\ninstead of a bespoke tree comparator, and doubles as exercise of `reconcile.ts` against list/\ntask-list shapes it hasn't been run against yet.",
    "title": "00C64YWTRG017",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG018",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG018",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Run against every real artifact in `AperasKG/artifacts/` (not just the synthetic sample): 9 of\n11 round-trip with zero added/removed. The other 2 each produce exactly one added+removed pair,\nboth explained by §1's canonical-not-byte-exact choice rather than a bug:",
    "title": "00C64YWTRG018",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG019",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG019",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG01A",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG01C"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C64YWTRG019",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG01A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG01A",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG01B"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWTRG01A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG01B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG01B",
    "children": [],
    "text": "A nested `code` fence whose original *absolute* indentation was deeper than the minimal\n  amount its list item requires (source used 4 spaces where 2 would do) re-projects at the\n  canonical 2 — the code's own *relative* internal formatting is preserved, only the baseline\n  shifts, but that's still a different `text`, so exact-key Stage A correctly doesn't match it.",
    "title": "00C64YWTRG01B",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG01C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG01C",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG01D"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWTRG01C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWTRG01D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWTRG01D",
    "children": [],
    "text": "An indented-style code block converts to fenced-style on projection (§5) — a real, disclosed\n  change to the stored `text`, so it doesn't match either, for the same reason.\n  Both are accepted per the same \"precision over recall\" principle reconciliation already uses\n  elsewhere (§2 of the reconciliation design) — a wrong same-content guess is worse than a\n  visible remove+add.",
    "title": "00C64YWTRG01D",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX5G010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX5G010",
    "children": [],
    "text": "*Aperis* (Latin verb meaning “open, uncover”): The open-source act of laying knowledge bare, mirroring its legal fluidity under [The Unlicense](https://unlicense.org/) by refusing rigid cages or ownership.",
    "title": "00C64YWX5G010",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX6000D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX6000D",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX6000E"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWX6000D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX6000E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX6000E",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Mirrored bidirectionally as plain JSON-LD files under `AperasKG/Apeiron/` (`Aperas-architecture.md` §5) — a portable, engine-agnostic round-trip of the same content, independent of TerminusDB's own storage internals.",
    "title": "00C64YWX6000E",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX6004F",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004G",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004H"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWX6004F",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX6004G",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Phase 4: Substrate Evolution — ApeironNgn (native Rust successor, speculative)",
    "title": "00C64YWX6004G",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX6004H",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004J",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004S",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX60050",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX60057"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C64YWX6004H",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX6004J",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004K",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004M"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWX6004J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX6004K",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Motivation: right-sizing the substrate to what Aperas actually exercises",
    "title": "00C64YWX6004K",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX6004M",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004N",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004Q"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C64YWX6004M",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX6004N",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004P"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWX6004N",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX6004P",
    "children": [],
    "text": "TerminusDB Community brings a general-purpose Prolog/WOQL Datalog engine, enterprise-oriented tooling, and its own bundle/layer format for versioning — capability well beyond what Phase 0-3 skills exercise (document CRUD, one-hop impact traversal, branch/commit/merge as a review workflow).",
    "title": "00C64YWX6004P",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX6004Q",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004R"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWX6004Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX6004R",
    "children": [],
    "text": "The bidirectional JSON-LD mirror (`AperasKG/Apeiron/`, `Aperas-architecture.md` §5) demonstrates this directly: the canonical graph content already round-trips as plain JSON-LD files, decoupled from TerminusDB's own storage internals — nothing about the substrate's actual content depends on TerminusDB being the engine underneath it.",
    "title": "00C64YWX6004R",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX6004S",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004T",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004V"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWX6004S",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX6004T",
    "children": [],
    "text": "ApeironNgn: a minimal engine sized to exactly what Aperas needs",
    "title": "00C64YWX6004T",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX6004V",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004W",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004Y"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C64YWX6004V",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX6004W",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004X"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWX6004W",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX6004X",
    "children": [],
    "text": "A small, embeddable Rust graph engine scoped to the primitives Phase 0-3 actually use: the `BaseNode`/`BaseLink`/`BaseEdge` document model and simple pattern-match queries (source/predicate/target lookups, bounded-depth traversal) — no general Datalog/Prolog solver, no auto-generated GraphQL schema, no multi-tenant/enterprise surface.",
    "title": "00C64YWX6004X",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX6004Y",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004Z"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWX6004Y",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX6004Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX6004Z",
    "children": [],
    "text": "No separate commit-layer engine to build: `AperasKG/Apeiron/` already lives inside a real git repository, so a JSON-LD write followed by an ordinary `git commit` over that directory *is* the version control — immutable history, diffing, and branching all come from git itself, not a bespoke bundle/layer format ApeironNgn would otherwise have to reimplement. TerminusDB needed its own commit-layer machinery because it owns an opaque store with no git underneath it; once Aperas is managing history directly against `AperasKG/Apeiron/`, ApeironNgn doesn't need to.",
    "title": "00C64YWX6004Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX60050",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX60050",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX60051",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX60052"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWX60050",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX60051",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX60051",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Migration surface: the same modules stand in for the same role, one changing shape",
    "title": "00C64YWX60051",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX60052",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX60052",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX60053",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX60055"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C64YWX60052",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX60053",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX60053",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX60054"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWX60053",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX60054",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX60054",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`client.ts`, `crud.ts`, `woql.ts`, and `graphql.ts` (`Aperas-architecture.md` §3) already isolate every TerminusDB-specific call behind a small, named set of modules — that boundary is what ApeironNgn would need to implement to stand in for TerminusDB, with `AperasKG/Apeiron/` as the on-disk state `kg:export`/`kg:import` already round-trip through.",
    "title": "00C64YWX60054",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX60055",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX60055",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX60056"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWX60055",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX60056",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX60056",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`versionControl.ts` doesn't carry over as-is — its branch/commit/diff/merge calls would delegate straight to real `git` operations on the `AperasKG` repository instead of TerminusDB's git-like API, since the KG's \"commit\" *is* a git commit once ApeironNgn is the engine.",
    "title": "00C64YWX60056",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX60057",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX60057",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX60058",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX60059"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWX60057",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX60058",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX60058",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Status: unscheduled and speculative",
    "title": "00C64YWX60058",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX60059",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX60059",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX6005A"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C64YWX60059",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX6005A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX6005A",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX6005B"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWX6005A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX6005B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX6005B",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Contingent on Phase 0-3 confirming that TerminusDB Community edition's rough edges — cross-store `bundle`/`unbundle` incompatibility (`terminusdb/terminusdb#2509`) and the `List`-typed `@unfold` gap (`terminusdb/terminusdb#2512`), both documented in `Aperas-dev-status.md` — are structural rather than incidental before committing engineering effort to a replacement.",
    "title": "00C64YWX6005B",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX6802Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX6802Q",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX6802R",
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX6802S"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWX6802Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX6802R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX6802R",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Future substrate alternative under consideration",
    "title": "00C64YWX6802R",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX6802S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX6802S",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX6802T"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C64YWX6802S",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX6802T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX6802T",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YWX6802V"
    ],
    "title": "00C64YWX6802T",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YWX6802V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YWX6802V",
    "children": [],
    "text": "ApeironNgn — a minimal Rust graph engine scoped to exactly what Aperas exercises — is sketched as a speculative future replacement; see Development Roadmap \"Phase 4: Substrate Evolution\".",
    "title": "00C64YWX6802V",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT000Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT000Q",
    "children": [],
    "text": "KG backup/restore — `restore.sh`/`tdb-log.sh`/`tdb-doc.sh` relocated to `Aperas/scripts/` and re-scoped as Core-Engine infra (documented in `Aperas-architecture.md` §1/§8), not domain-KG-specific — `db/` itself is gone from `AperasKG/`. `tdb-cross-diff.sh` was *not* migrated with them (its own hash-gated rewrite was already pending the ID-identity fix); genuinely gone, not relocated.",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB000P",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT000S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT000S",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**RESOLVED** Design issue: \"AperasKG stores the KG\" was answered with a DB backup, not a KG export — corrected",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB000R",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT000T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT000T",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT000V",
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT000X",
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT000Z"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C64Z9NB000S",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT000V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT000V",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT000W"
    ],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB000T",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT000W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT000W",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`AperasKG` was designed to hold both the domain artifacts and the KG itself, but the KG lives in a DB — so the earlier approach to fulfilling that second half was to associate whole-TerminusDB-volume/bundle backups (`restore.sh`, briefly stored under `AperasKG/db/`) with the domain-KG repo. That coupling was the wrong move: a git-tracked repo has no good way to diff, merge, or meaningfully version an opaque binary DB snapshot, and (per the `#2509` investigation above) those snapshots turned out not to even be portable between independent TerminusDB stores — so it wasn't a viable backup path for `AperasKG` even setting the git-coupling problem aside.",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB000V",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT000X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT000X",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT000Y"
    ],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB000W",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT000Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT000Y",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Corrected via the JSON-LD import/export round-trip (`web/src/lib/export.ts`, `kg:export`/`kg:import`, `Aperas-architecture.md` §5): `AperasKG/Apeiron/` holds the canonical graph content as plain, diffable JSON-LD text, committed to the same repo as `AperasKG/artifacts/` — an ordinary `git commit` over that directory is now the KG's backup, `kg:import` is the restore path.",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB000X",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT000Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT000Z",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT0010"
    ],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB000Y",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT0010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT0010",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`restore.sh`'s whole-volume/bundle mechanism (§6) is unaffected and stays as-is — it's TerminusDB server infrastructure (Docker-volume disaster recovery), a different, unrelated concern from how `AperasKG` records its own content. Likewise, the SSH-tunneled TerminusDB remotes (§7) are unrelated to `AperasKG` — that's cross-machine sync for the TerminusDB server itself, not something this redesign touches.",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB000Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT0019",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT0019",
    "children": [],
    "text": "The legacy flat `DocumentNode` / `BlockNode` / `SpanNode` schema was entirely eliminated.",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB0018",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT001B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT001B",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Designed and implemented a universal, recursive `BlockNode` topology (Fractal Ontology) rooted in `ArtifactNode`.",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB001A",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT001D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT001D",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Schema updated to pure JSON-LD (`schema.json`), avoiding TypeScript interface duplication.",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB001C",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT001F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT001F",
    "children": [],
    "text": "IDs & content fingerprint — **implemented and live-verified** (`Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §1). `web/src/lib/snowflake.ts` generates the 64-bit Snowflake-style identifier (timestamp + machine identity w/ personal failover + sequence counter, 13-char Crockford Base32); `astParser.ts` uses it for every `blockId` instead of the old content hash. `ArtifactNode.contentHash` renamed to `fileHash` throughout (`artifacts.ts`, `schema.json`) to match §1.B's file-domain-only fingerprint — no structural/recursive hash. Verified live: cleared stale pre-redesign `ArtifactNode`/`BlockNode` docs, ran `kg:track`+`kg:ingest` across all 8 artifacts (1144 blocks total, including a 648-block single-artifact burst), zero id collisions. Also found and fixed a real pre-existing bug while verifying: `getArtifactRecord` treated a missing document's raw 404 response (a string, not a thrown error) as a valid record, so untracked artifacts silently reported \"unchanged\" instead of erroring. Reconciliation (best-effort content matching, §1.C history in Appendix F) remains unimplemented — no code needed it yet, since ingestion so far has only ever run against uningested artifacts.",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB001E",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT001G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT001G",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT001H"
    ],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB001F",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT001H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT001H",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Ingestion (`astParser.ts` and `artifacts.ts`) now parses Markdown into a deeply nested tree structure and commits the entire fractal tree via `ArtifactNode.root` in a single TerminusDB operation. Note: a plain `getDocument` read only ever returns `root`/`children` as reference ids, not the nested tree, so full-tree reads go through `getArtifactTreeViaGraphQL` (`graphql.ts`) instead — deliberately, not because the Document API is incapable of it (see `Aperas-architecture.md` §2's \"Read-path note\" for the full investigation, including a filed upstream bug, [terminusdb/terminusdb#2512](https://github.com/terminusdb/terminusdb/issues/2512)).",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB001G",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT001J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT001J",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT001K"
    ],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB001H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT001K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT001K",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`FolderNode` — **implemented and live-verified** (`Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §4.A). `web/src/lib/folders.ts` walks `AperasKG/artifacts/`, builds one `FolderNode` per directory, absorbs each directory's own `README.md` (parsed blocks become the folder's children; the file itself is never exposed as a separate `ArtifactNode`), and references nested `FolderNode`s/`ArtifactNode`s by id. Wired into `npm run kg:ingest`, which now rebuilds the whole folder tree in the same run as artifact ingestion. Added one concrete `Assertion` class (inherits the previously-uninstantiable abstract `BaseEdge`) to `schema.json`, needed to let `crud.ts`/`woql.ts` actually write/query extrinsic edges — documented in `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §2.D. `FolderNode`/`ArtifactNode` are now Snowflake-keyed (`folderId`/`artifactId`), `path` a plain mutable field — see the \"Reconciliation matching\" entry below for the full migration.",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB001J",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT001M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT001M",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT001N"
    ],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB8000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT001N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT001N",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`crud.ts`/`woql.ts`/`graphql.ts`/`verifyPhase0.ts` — **migrated off the dead pre-redesign schema and live-verified**. `crud.ts` now provides `insertAssertion`/`deleteAssertionsInvolvingNode` for the new `Assertion` type; `woql.ts` queries `Assertion.source`/`predicate`/`target` (node-typed, not the old flat `xsd:string` `subjectId`/`objectId`) in both directions plus one-hop impact propagation; `graphql.ts` replaced the removed `docId`-scoped block query with `getArtifactTreeViaGraphQL` (bounded-depth nested `root`/`children` selection — GraphQL has no native recursion, so depth is generated explicitly, default 10). `verifyPhase0.ts` was rewritten into a full idempotent, self-cleaning live test of the whole pipeline (AST parsing → track/ingest → GraphQL tree read → `FolderNode` ingestion → `Assertion` CRUD + WOQL traversal → temporal commit management); `npm run verify:phase0 -- --db` and `npm run build` both confirmed passing.",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB8001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT001P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT001P",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT001Q"
    ],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB8002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT001Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT001Q",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Discovered while wiring this up**: TerminusDB enforces referential integrity on document delete — deleting a still-referenced document (e.g. an `ArtifactNode` still listed in a `FolderNode.children`, or a `BlockNode` still pointed to by `ArtifactNode.root`) fails with a `SchemaCheckFailure`, not silently. The best-effort delete helpers in `crud.ts` (`deleteDocumentIfExists`/`deleteDocumentsIfExist`) used to swallow *all* errors on the assumption only \"not found\" could occur — that assumption was wrong and masked this failure mode; they now log instead of swallowing silently, and any caller managing referenced state (like `verifyPhase0.ts`'s cleanup) has to delete in reverse-reference order.",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB8003",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT001R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT001R",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT001S"
    ],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB8004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT001S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT001S",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Heading levels now define tree structure** — **implemented and live-verified**. `astParser.ts` gained `groupByHeadings`, a one-pass depth-stack transform run on every flat mdast sibling list before conversion: each heading becomes the parent of everything until a heading of depth <= its own. A doc with `# Title` / `## Section A` / `## Section B` now parses as nested (`Title` containing `Section A`, `Section B`, each with their own body), not a flat list under the root. Alongside this: every `BlockNode` now carries its raw mdast `type` (needed by reconciliation's leaf/container split below), and `list`/`listItem`/`blockquote` no longer carry the full-subtree-duplicate `text` they used to (confirmed live pre-fix: a `listItem`'s `text` byte-for-byte duplicated its own paragraph child's) — containers now carry no content of their own, by design.",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB8005",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT001T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT001T",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT001V"
    ],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB8006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT001V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT001V",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Reconciliation matching for re-ingestion** — **implemented and live-verified** (`Aperas-reconciliation-matching-design.md`, `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §1.B/§4.A/§4.B/Appendix G). New `web/src/lib/reconcile.ts`: a Gestalt (Ratcliff/Obershelp) tree diff — the longest-common-run algorithm behind Python's `difflib` — applied two-stage per level (Stage A anchors on leaf content by `heading XOR text`; Stage B aligns containers by type within the segments Stage A's anchors define), with ambiguous same-content duplicates declined rather than guessed. Matched `BlockNode`s reuse their old `blockId`; unmatched old ones get an explicit `tombstonedAt` (new field on `BaseNode`, inherited everywhere) rather than being silently orphaned; a block relocated to a different section is detected as a cross-parent move via the same mechanism, one level up from per-parent matching. `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode` moved off `Lexical`-on-`path` to Snowflake ids (`artifactId`/`folderId`, same scheme as `BlockNode.blockId`), `path` now a plain mutable field with `title`/`text` added to `ArtifactNode` (filename / naive first-paragraph abstract, matching `FolderNode`'s existing shape) — this is what makes a file/folder rename a field update instead of a delete-and-recreate. Rename detection reuses the identical Gestalt-matching primitive one level up: on every `kg:track`/`kg:ingest` sweep, disk-only and DB-only leftover paths are matched by abstract-text similarity (`matchLeftoverByAbstract`) before falling back to plain add/remove. Wired into `ingestArtifact` (fires whenever a prior ingestion exists), `trackAllArtifacts`, and `ingestFolderTree`; `kgCli.ts` reports renamed/removed/reconciled counts alongside the existing tracked/ingested counts. Live-verified via `verifyPhase0.ts` (edit-and-reingest keeps unrelated `blockId`s stable, reports sane unchanged/added counts) and a manual rename test against a throwaway artifact (`artifactId` and `blockId`s survived a real on-disk move). Migrating the key scheme required clearing all pre-existing `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode`/`BlockNode` documents first, since TerminusDB rejects a schema whose new required fields the old instance data doesn't have — the whole KG was then rebuilt from `AperasKG/artifacts/` via a full `kg:track` + `kg:ingest` sweep, per the project's disk-is-source-of-truth model.",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB8007",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT001Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT001Y",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT001Z",
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT0021",
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT0023",
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT0025"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C64Z9NB800C",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT001Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT001Z",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT0020"
    ],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB800D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT0020",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT0020",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Fractal Ontology Enhancements** (`Aperas-fractal-ontology-implementation-plan.md` Stage 2, items 4-5): AI-driven summarization during ingestion (splitting blocks intelligently into `title` vs `text`) and structural extraction of inline Markdown links into `BaseLink` edges. Confirmed still unimplemented: `astParser.ts`'s `isStructural` node-type list doesn't even include `link`, so inline Markdown links are currently just silently absorbed into the parent block's raw `text`, not extracted at all.",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB800E",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT0021",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT0021",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64Z9NB800G"
    ],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB800F",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT0022",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT0022",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Projection Engines (Phase 1)**: three modes per `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §5.A — Artifact Projection (serialize a `BlockNode` tree back to its `.md` file) has a settled design in `Aperas-artifact-projection-design.md`, not yet implemented; the Human UI (SolidJS read-projection, 'Hover Preview' link mechanism, `unfolded` view-state) and the Agentic BFS interface remain undesigned.",
    "title": "00C64YXFT0022",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:03:13.965Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT0023",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT0023",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT0024"
    ],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB800H",
    "type": "listItem",
