  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT0028",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT0028",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT0029"
    ],
    "title": "## Appendix: cross-store `bundle`/`unbundle` incompatibility investigation",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT0029",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT0029",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002A",
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002C",
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002E",
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002G",
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002J",
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002M",
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002P",
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002R",
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002T",
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002W",
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002Y"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C64Z9NB800Q",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT002A",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002B"
    ],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB800R",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT002B",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Historical record — the `restore.sh`/`bundle` workflow this investigation covers predates its relocation to `Aperas/scripts/` (see \"KG backup/restore\" above); kept for reference in case a similar mechanism is reintroduced.",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB800S",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT002C",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002D"
    ],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB800T",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT002D",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Symptom: `aperas_apeiron_snapshot_A.bundle` (made on Host A) and `aperas_apeiron_snapshot_B.bundle` (made on Host B) each verify cleanly **only on their own origin machine**, and fail deterministically with `error(unknown_layer_reference(<hash>))` on the other — a different specific missing-layer hash each time.",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB800V",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT002E",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002F"
    ],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB800W",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT002F",
    "children": [],
    "text": "An earlier pass at this investigation, run on a single host in isolation, found a byte pattern in a snapshot that looked like Latin-1/UTF-8 mojibake corruption (reversing it produced a plausible gzip header) and concluded the file was corrupted. **That conclusion was wrong and has been retracted** — the same file was later shown to unbundle perfectly on its own origin host, which a genuinely corrupted file cannot do. The byte pattern was a coincidental artifact, not evidence of corruption.",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB800X",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT002G",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002H"
    ],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB800Y",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT002H",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Ruled out version mismatch: both machines confirmed running byte-identical `TerminusDB v12.0.7 (57f2093baeafd65e16004e84b7b58e0c5cf72858)` / `terminusdb-store v0.19.8`.",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB800Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT002J",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002K"
    ],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB8010",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT002K",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Ruled out the `auto-optimize` community plugin (`/plugins/auto-optimize.pl`, a probabilistic post-commit layer squash/GC): disabled on both machines (moved the plugin file out, restarted), re-tested with a brand-new minimal scratch database — still failed cross-host identically.",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB8011",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT002M",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002N"
    ],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB8012",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT002N",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Ruled out store \"age\": reproduced with a store `store init`'d seconds before the test, same as the destination.",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB8013",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT002P",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002Q"
    ],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB8014",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT002Q",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Decisive isolation, no second machine needed**: ran two independent TerminusDB containers (`terminusdb` and a throwaway `terminusdb-freshtest`, same image, same physical host, plugin off on both) and bundled/unbundled between them. Same failure. A positive control — unbundling the same file back into a *different database within its own originating container* — succeeded every time. This isolates the variable precisely: **it's not host A vs. host B, or even separate machines at all — it's any two independent TerminusDB stores (server instances/storage directories), even side-by-side on one host.**",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB8015",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT002R",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002S"
    ],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB8016",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT002S",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Cross-checked against prior art: [terminusdb/terminusdb#1147](https://github.com/terminusdb/terminusdb/issues/1147) reports the identical symptom moving a bundle between two instances, never reproduced by the maintainer, closed stale/not-planned. [terminusdb/terminusdb#1235](https://github.com/terminusdb/terminusdb/pull/1235) (\"an initial effort to figure out #1147 without success\") added CLI bundle/unbundle tests that call `store.init()` exactly once and share that one store across every test — so its test suite never actually exercises the cross-store case, which is the one that fails.",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB8017",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT002T",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002V"
    ],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB8018",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT002V",
    "children": [],
    "text": "The official [\"move a database between servers\" backup/restore guide](https://terminusdb.org/docs/enterprise-backup-restore/) is scoped to **Enterprise edition** (different mechanism: `/api/bundle` + `/api/unbundle` REST endpoints, target pre-created) — not a documented guarantee for the Community-edition CLI commands we're using.",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB8019",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT002W",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002X"
    ],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB801A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT002X",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Filed as [terminusdb/terminusdb#2509](https://github.com/terminusdb/terminusdb/issues/2509), including the two-store repro and a note about the test-coverage gap in #1235. Draft/record kept at `terminusdb-issue-bundle-cross-store.md`.",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB801B",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT002Y",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002Z"
    ],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB801C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YXFT002Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YXFT002Z",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Conclusion for this project: `bundle`/`unbundle`/`restore.sh` remain valid for same-store snapshot/rollback, but are not to be relied on for cross-machine transfer.",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB801D",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YY0C000J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YY0C000J",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Info:**",
    "title": "00C64YY0C000J",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YY0C000Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YY0C000Z",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Additional context**\nTraced the actual root cause into `src/rust/terminusdb-community/src/doc/mod.rs`. For TerminusDB v12, a single-document `doc get` doesn't go through `json.pl`'s `get_document`/`get_document_` at all — it goes through the Rust foreign predicate `print_document_json`, which calls `DocumentContext::get_id_document`. That's where field-level `@unfold` is actually decided, via a `(parent_type_id, predicate_id)` pair (`unfold_pairs`) read off the *enclosing* stack frame:",
    "title": "00C64YY0C000Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YY0C0010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YY0C0010",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```rust\nlet field_level_unfold = match (parent_type_id, predicate_id) {\n    (Some(pt), Some(pr)) => self.unfold_pairs.contains(&(pt, pr)),\n    _ => false,\n};\n```",
    "title": "00C64YY0C0010",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YY0C0011",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YY0C0011",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`parent_type_id`/`predicate_id` come from `StackEntry::document_type_id()` / `current_predicate()`:",
    "title": "00C64YY0C0011",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YY0C0012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YY0C0012",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```rust\nfn document_type_id(&self) -> Option<u64> {\n    match self {\n        Self::Document { type_id, .. } => *type_id,\n        _ => None,\n    }\n}\n\nfn current_predicate(&mut self) -> Option<u64> {\n    match self {\n        Self::Document { fields, .. } => fields.as_mut().and_then(|f| f.peek().map(|t| t.predicate)),\n        _ => None,\n    }\n}\n```",
    "title": "00C64YY0C0012",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YY0C0015",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YY0C0015",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`Set`/`Optional`/`Cardinality` values sit as direct triples on the document, so the enclosing frame is always `StackEntry::Document`, and both lookups succeed — this is why they work.",
    "title": "00C64YY0C0015",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YY0C0017",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YY0C0017",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`List` and `Array` values instead sit behind an intermediate `StackEntry::List` / `StackEntry::Array` frame (the RDF Cons chain for `List`, the array's index triples for `Array`), pushed onto the traversal stack while the document's field is walked. Neither variant carries the parent document's type/predicate forward, so `document_type_id()`/`current_predicate()` fall through the wildcard arm above and return `None` for anything nested inside a `List` or `Array` — silently disabling field-level `@unfold` for their elements regardless of what the schema says.",
    "title": "00C64YY0C0017",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YY0C0019",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YY0C0019",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Class-level `@unfoldable` keeps working regardless, because it's checked via `self.unfoldables.contains(&t.object)`, which only needs the target's own type, not the enclosing frame.",
    "title": "00C64YY0C0019",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64YY0C001D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64YY0C001D",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Fix**\nCapture the parent's `type_id`/`predicate_id` before pushing the `List`/`Array` frame and thread it through `StackEntry::List` and `ArrayStackEntry` so nested elements still match against `unfold_pairs`. Verified against a from-source build: the fix compiles, all existing Rust unit tests still pass, `cargo clippy` shows no new warnings, and new integration tests for `List` retrieval and a 2D `Array` case (added to `tests/test/field-level-unfold.js`, per the request in [the maintainer reply](https://github.com/terminusdb/terminusdb/issues/2512#issuecomment-5463157961)) pass against a live server built from the fix.",
    "title": "00C64YY0C001D",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64Z9NB8008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64Z9NB8008",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C64Z9NB8009"
    ],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB8008",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64Z9NB8009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64Z9NB8009",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Artifact Projection** — **implemented and live-verified** (`Aperas-artifact-projection-design.md`, `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §5.A mode 1 of 3). New `web/src/lib/project.ts` serializes an `ArtifactNode`'s ingested `BlockNode` tree back into Markdown — canonical regeneration, not byte-exact: headings/paragraphs/code round-trip via their raw `title`/`text`, while `list`/`blockquote` are regenerated as clean Markdown (list items always blank-line-separated regardless of original tight/loose style; blockquote `> ` re-prefixed uniformly rather than trusting what the raw text happens to carry). Needed two new captured fields on `BlockNode` — `ordered`/`start` (list numbering) and `checked` (task-list checkbox) — both `Optional`, so unlike the `artifactId`/`type` migration this needed no DB wipe. Exposed via `npm run kg:project -- <path>`. Verified two ways: `verifyPhase0.ts`'s synthetic sample (every branch: ordered/unordered/task lists, nested list, blockquote, code) round-trips with zero drift by reusing `reconcile.ts`'s own matcher as the equivalence check; and, more usefully, running the same check against all 11 real artifacts in `AperasKG/artifacts/` surfaced two genuine bugs no synthetic sample had exercised — a nested code fence's closing `` ``` `` desyncing from its opening one because only a multi-line leaf's *first* line has container-required indentation stripped (every later line keeps its literal original-file column; fixed with a `dedent` normalization), and an *indented* (4-space) code block silently degrading into an ordinary paragraph because its raw slice carries no fence to re-emit (fixed by re-fencing it). After those two fixes, 9 of 11 real artifacts round-trip with zero drift; the other 2 each show one accepted, disclosed difference (absolute code-indentation depth normalized to the minimum; indented-style converted to fenced-style) — real content changes under exact-key matching, not bugs, per the design doc §8.",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB8009",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C64Z9NB800G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C64Z9NB800G",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Projection Engines (Phase 1)**: three modes per `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §5.A. The Human UI (SolidJS read-projection, 'Hover Preview' link mechanism, `unfolded` view-state) and the Agentic BFS interface remain undesigned.",
    "title": "00C64Z9NB800G",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  }
]
